WEBVTT

00:00.008 --> 00:35.166
Support Admin Watch on
kissasia.cam or kisskh.org

01:19.044 --> 01:21.909
-(WOMAN GASPS)
-(TIRES SCREECHING)

01:21.978 --> 01:23.181
(SIGHS IN RELIEF)

01:29.249 --> 01:30.551
(TIRES SCREECHING)

01:34.824 --> 01:35.823
Oh, shit!

01:35.892 --> 01:36.887
(HORN BLARING)

01:38.158 --> 01:39.131
(PHONE CHIMES)

01:43.360 --> 01:44.433
Oh, fuck!

01:56.881 --> 01:59.118
(TIRES SCREECHING)

02:08.688 --> 02:10.657
<i> (THE NEW POLLUTION</i>
BY BECK PLAYING)

02:21.107 --> 02:23.541
This the line
for There Will Be Buns?

02:23.610 --> 02:25.373
You know it.

02:25.442 --> 02:27.009
Any idea how long
the wait's supposed to be?

02:27.078 --> 02:29.510
Uh, they said
about two hours.

02:29.579 --> 02:31.907
Wow. That's a long time
to wait for cinnamon buns.

02:31.976 --> 02:33.710
Is this your first bun?
They're incredible.

02:33.778 --> 02:35.577
I'm actually not
that big on sweets.

02:35.645 --> 02:37.354
Then why are you here?

02:38.219 --> 02:40.083
Oh, I'm on TaskSergeant.

02:40.152 --> 02:42.593
I'm actually getting paid to
wait in line for someone else.

02:42.662 --> 02:43.954
Hmm, that...

02:44.663 --> 02:46.192
sucks ass.

02:46.260 --> 02:47.326
Did you go to college?

02:47.394 --> 02:49.658
Uh, yeah, I went to college.

02:49.727 --> 02:51.432
Then why are you
a laundryman?

02:51.501 --> 02:53.872
I'm not a laundryman.
I'm doing TaskSergeant.

02:53.941 --> 02:56.505
Did you not do good
in college?

02:56.573 --> 02:59.034
ARJ:<i> Hey. Yeah, I'm still</i>
<i> waiting on those buns.</i>

02:59.103 --> 03:01.013
<i> They said it should probably</i>
<i> be another hour.</i>

03:01.081 --> 03:02.209
What do you want to be
when you grow up?

03:02.278 --> 03:03.611
I want to be an archeologist.

03:03.679 --> 03:05.049
ARJ: You want me to tell you
how that's going to go?

03:05.117 --> 03:06.610
You're going
to major in archeology,

03:06.679 --> 03:07.943
and then you're going
to get out

03:08.012 --> 03:10.746
and there's going to be
no archeology jobs.

03:10.815 --> 03:12.057
I've been an adult
a long time.

03:12.125 --> 03:13.920
You know how many
archeologists I've met?

03:13.988 --> 03:14.985
Zero.

03:16.961 --> 03:18.890
Okay, Arnold, meet...

03:19.765 --> 03:20.890
your new desk.

03:20.958 --> 03:23.635
<i> So now you got no job,</i>
<i> a useless degree,</i>

03:23.704 --> 03:24.933
and a ton of debt.

03:25.002 --> 03:26.270
What happens then?

03:26.339 --> 03:28.971
Well, I hope you like it here,
'cause guess what?

03:29.039 --> 03:30.070
You're moving back home!

03:30.139 --> 03:31.570
You need some money.

03:31.639 --> 03:33.276
<i> So you start</i>
<i> doing TaskSergeant.</i>

03:33.345 --> 03:35.374
<i> You take every part-time gig</i>
<i> you can get.</i>

03:35.443 --> 03:36.705
<i> You're working all the time.</i>

03:36.773 --> 03:38.379
<i> But you never have enough.</i>

03:38.447 --> 03:40.249
I know you got
a lot of big hopes.

03:40.318 --> 03:42.119
I used to be
a little Indian kid, too.

03:42.187 --> 03:44.284
But I got news for you,
little man.

03:44.352 --> 03:48.153
The American dream is dead.

03:48.222 --> 03:50.393
(PHONE CHIMES)

03:50.462 --> 03:52.729
Yeah, I probably shouldn't
have said that stuff.

03:52.798 --> 03:54.593
So sorry, guys.

03:54.661 --> 03:57.300
-All out for the day.
-MAN: What?

03:57.369 --> 04:00.334
I'm going to fuck this place
with one star.

04:00.403 --> 04:03.802
Hey, it's Arj
from TaskSergeant.

04:03.871 --> 04:08.003
Uh, I'm so sorry,
they actually sold out of buns.

04:08.072 --> 04:09.441
Yeah, you won't get charged
for the buns,

04:09.510 --> 04:11.641
but please don't
cancel the task.

04:11.710 --> 04:12.975
'Cause then I don't get paid,

04:13.044 --> 04:15.350
and, you know, I did
wait, like, two hours.

04:15.418 --> 04:18.582
Okay. Thanks
for understanding. Bye.

04:18.651 --> 04:20.319
-MAN: There are my buns!
-Hey.

04:20.387 --> 04:22.325
Yo. Thank you so much.

04:22.394 --> 04:24.126
-WOMAN: Sure.
-Ooh. The bag's still warm.

04:24.195 --> 04:27.329
-Love it. See you soon.
-See ya.

04:27.398 --> 04:29.031
Who's that guy?
How'd he get some buns?

04:29.100 --> 04:30.800
He's one of our investors.

04:30.869 --> 04:31.864
(PHONE CHIMES)

04:34.566 --> 04:35.667
Canceled? (GRUMBLES)

04:35.736 --> 04:37.632
You said you weren't
going to do that!

04:37.701 --> 04:38.974
Goddamn it, David H!

04:39.043 --> 04:40.873
(TSKS) Fuck my life.

04:56.195 --> 04:59.525
Hey. Can I talk
to you for a second?

04:59.594 --> 05:01.624
-ARJ: Sure.
-Elena from lumber.

05:01.692 --> 05:03.234
Arj, floor associate.

05:03.302 --> 05:05.995
-Sometimes power tools.
-(ELENA CHUCKLES)

05:06.064 --> 05:08.604
Are you happy with
the work environment here?

05:09.543 --> 05:10.575
No.

05:10.643 --> 05:12.541
Exactly.

05:12.610 --> 05:14.676
I mean, we know they can do
so much better here,

05:14.744 --> 05:17.377
(SOFTLY) and that's why
I'm trying to start a union.

05:17.446 --> 05:18.845
I'm just
working here part-time

05:18.914 --> 05:21.178
-to save some money
and then I'm moving on.
-Okay.

05:21.247 --> 05:22.747
Well, just because you're not
going to be somewhere forever

05:22.816 --> 05:24.620
doesn't mean
you can't make it better.

05:25.892 --> 05:26.853
Nothing ever changes.

05:27.993 --> 05:29.385
So what's your answer?

05:29.453 --> 05:30.593
Give up?

05:31.790 --> 05:34.190
-I don't have an answer.
-Hmm.

05:35.826 --> 05:40.471
Okay, Arj, floor associate,

05:42.007 --> 05:43.540
best of luck to you.

05:49.683 --> 05:50.679
Thank you.

05:52.743 --> 05:55.219
ELENA: Smelling good.

05:55.288 --> 05:58.790
Oh. You guys are
out of suadero. Damn!

05:58.859 --> 06:00.354
Suadero's my jam.

06:00.423 --> 06:03.590
Um, okay.
Have a good night.

06:03.659 --> 06:06.288
Hey. I got four.
You want some of mine?

06:07.660 --> 06:08.726
-Yeah.
-ARJ: All right.

06:08.795 --> 06:11.026
Come over here,
Elena from lumber.

06:11.095 --> 06:13.029
-You cool with these fixings?
-I am.

06:13.098 --> 06:14.271
I went a little heavy
on the green sauce.

06:14.339 --> 06:16.441
-Is that okay?
-That's always good.

06:16.510 --> 06:18.910
So how you been sleeping, man?
You look a little tired.

06:18.979 --> 06:20.935
Wow, thanks for noticing.

06:21.004 --> 06:22.207
It's a new look
I'm going for.

06:22.275 --> 06:23.578
Sorry.

06:23.647 --> 06:25.545
Uh, no, I haven't been
sleeping that well.

06:25.614 --> 06:27.744
-You got any tips?
-Actually, I do.

06:27.813 --> 06:29.085
I've been using
sleep stories

06:29.153 --> 06:30.453
-on my phone.
-Oh.

06:30.521 --> 06:31.883
Pretty much I just
listen to this guy talk,

06:31.951 --> 06:33.555
and he's so boring
that I just knock out.

06:33.623 --> 06:35.383
-I gotta give it a try.
-Works every time.

06:35.452 --> 06:37.154
So what do you do all day
when you're so well-rested?

06:38.460 --> 06:39.893
-I make furniture.
-Oh.

06:39.962 --> 06:41.595
Yeah, that's why I started
working at Hardware Heaven

06:41.664 --> 06:43.132
so I can get some
of those discounts.

06:43.201 --> 06:44.494
-Mmm.
-What about you?

06:44.563 --> 06:45.595
What do you do?

06:45.664 --> 06:46.964
Um, I'm an editor.

06:47.032 --> 06:49.307
I edit documentaries,
things like that.

06:49.376 --> 06:51.309
I love documentaries.
What you working on now?

06:51.378 --> 06:53.641
Right now, I'm just
doing freelance stuff.

06:53.709 --> 06:55.511
I'm hoping to get
another proper gig soon.

06:55.580 --> 06:57.740
You'll get another one.
Keep your dreams alive.

06:57.808 --> 06:58.910
ARJ: I once dated a girl

06:58.978 --> 07:00.415
that had that tattooed
on her lower back.

07:00.484 --> 07:01.648
ELENA: Oh, yeah?
Where is she now?

07:01.716 --> 07:03.046
ARJ: I think
she's dating this DJ.

07:03.115 --> 07:05.652
ANGEL:<i> Elena,</i>
<i> with the cinnamon bun guy?</i>

07:05.720 --> 07:07.490
ELENA: Have you
ever been to a rave?

07:07.559 --> 07:09.325
-ARJ: No, I haven't.
-Don't take the drugs.

07:09.394 --> 07:11.021
I think I'll just
take the drugs

07:11.090 --> 07:12.659
-and just not go to the rave.
-(ELENA LAUGHS)

07:12.727 --> 07:14.931
-What about that option?
-Love that.

07:15.000 --> 07:16.864
(ELENA LAUGHS)

07:35.017 --> 07:36.917
MAN: (OVER PHONE)<i> Hey,</i>
<i> how is the new apartment?</i>

07:38.122 --> 07:41.053
Um, it's cozy.

07:41.121 --> 07:44.522
<i> Great, great. I was</i>
<i> talking to Ayesha Auntie.</i>

07:44.590 --> 07:48.363
<i> Your little cousin Naveen</i>
<i> got a really good job</i>
<i> with Microsoft.</i>

07:48.431 --> 07:50.626
<i> He's making lot of money.</i>

07:50.695 --> 07:52.227
Good for Naveen.

07:52.295 --> 07:55.702
<i> Maybe he can help you</i>
<i> to get a job.</i>

07:55.771 --> 07:57.836
I'm an editor.
I work on documentaries.

07:57.904 --> 08:00.170
What am I going
to do at Microsoft?

08:00.239 --> 08:03.645
<i> Maybe you can do a documentary</i>
<i> about Naveen.</i>

08:03.714 --> 08:07.879
<i> He's very smart,</i>
<i> successful, well-dressed.</i>

08:07.947 --> 08:10.621
Okay. Um, well,
I'll think about it.

08:13.052 --> 08:15.390
WOMAN: (ON APP)
<i> Welcome to Sleep Town,</i>

08:15.459 --> 08:18.358
<i> the sleep assistance podcast.</i>

08:18.426 --> 08:24.766
<i> Now, slowly feel</i>
<i> each part of your body</i>
<i> shutting down for the day.</i>

08:24.835 --> 08:29.401
<i> Your feet, your lower legs,</i>
<i> your upper...</i>

08:29.470 --> 08:32.002
-(UPBEAT MUSIC PLAYING)
-WOMAN:<i> Want to hear the pod</i>
<i> with no ads?</i>

08:32.071 --> 08:34.909
<i> Go to our channel</i>
<i> and subscribe now.</i>

08:34.978 --> 08:38.841
<i> Get exclusive sleep stories,</i>
<i> meditations and more.</i>

08:38.909 --> 08:40.816
<i> Only $5.99 a month.</i>

08:51.354 --> 08:53.895
All right. Everyone,
let's gather around.

09:09.778 --> 09:12.941
And there he was,
this lost soul,

09:13.009 --> 09:14.881
his head in his hands,

09:14.950 --> 09:18.755
about to jump headfirst
into Niagara Falls.

09:19.819 --> 09:22.283
As he lurked over the edge,

09:22.352 --> 09:24.755
panic filled his eyes
as he thought,

09:24.824 --> 09:28.795
"Oh, no. Is this the end?"

09:28.864 --> 09:31.762
I put my arm on his shoulder
and said,

09:31.830 --> 09:34.395
"Kenneth, I'm an angel.

09:34.464 --> 09:38.002
"My name is Azrael.
I'm here to save you."

09:38.070 --> 09:41.646
I showed him
what he had to live for.

09:41.714 --> 09:45.613
Visions that reflected
the hope his life promised.

09:45.682 --> 09:48.146
Cheering his son
at a soccer game,

09:48.215 --> 09:52.115
holding his wife on the couch
on a lazy Sunday,

09:52.183 --> 09:54.692
playing in the park
with his dog...

09:55.995 --> 09:58.320
Shoelace.

09:58.389 --> 10:02.300
"I see now that my life
was precious as it was.

10:02.369 --> 10:05.334
"Thank you
for showing me my path.

10:05.403 --> 10:08.533
"You are a special angel."

10:08.602 --> 10:11.566
(ALL APPLAUDING)

10:12.375 --> 10:14.110
GABRIEL: Martha?

10:14.179 --> 10:15.803
Yes, Gabriel.

10:15.872 --> 10:19.612
Is there any way I can
have more meaningful
duties like Azrael?

10:19.680 --> 10:21.346
I want to guide people,

10:21.415 --> 10:24.755
I want to change their lives,
I want to save a lost soul.

10:26.220 --> 10:30.286
To save a lost soul,
you have to find a lost soul.

10:30.355 --> 10:32.791
Finding a lost soul
is not easy, Gabriel.

10:32.860 --> 10:35.496
And showing them a path is...

10:35.564 --> 10:37.196
Is incredibly difficult.

10:37.265 --> 10:40.867
But I saw a person today.
His job is waiting in line.

10:40.935 --> 10:42.804
He's ready to give up
on his life.

10:42.872 --> 10:46.202
But that's not your task,
is it, Gabriel?

10:46.271 --> 10:48.174
How's the texting
and driving going?

10:48.243 --> 10:52.140
(SIGHS SOFTLY) It's a lot.
People really love doing it.

10:52.208 --> 10:53.980
What do you have this week?

10:54.049 --> 10:56.411
Um, I'm supposed to save
a woman named Elena,

10:56.480 --> 10:58.489
who works at a place
called Hardware Heaven.

10:58.558 --> 11:01.693
She almost backs
into a telephone pole.

11:01.761 --> 11:03.720
But you're not going to let
that happen, are you?

11:03.789 --> 11:05.855
No, I'm not.

11:05.924 --> 11:07.094
One step at a time.

11:09.660 --> 11:11.670
<i> (STREETS OF YOUR TOWN</i>
BY THE GO-BETWEENS PLAYING)

11:14.503 --> 11:16.037
Yeah. Uh...

11:19.178 --> 11:22.714
-(PA BUZZES)
-WOMAN ON PA:<i> Customer service</i>
<i> needed in plumbing.</i>

11:24.207 --> 11:25.975
<i> ♪ Round and round ♪</i>

11:26.043 --> 11:27.475
<i> ♪ Up and down ♪</i>

11:27.544 --> 11:29.953
<i> ♪ Through the streets</i>
<i> of your town ♪</i>

11:30.022 --> 11:31.954
GUARD: Lot's for
customers only, sir.
You can't sleep here.

11:32.023 --> 11:34.685
ARJ: I know. I was just
about to go get some groceries.

11:34.754 --> 11:37.562
Really? Looks like
you covered up your windows
and went to sleep.

11:37.630 --> 11:38.958
I know that's what
it looks like, but...

11:39.027 --> 11:41.064
Don't let me catch you
out here again.

11:41.132 --> 11:42.458
Okay.

11:42.527 --> 11:43.658
<i> ♪ And don't the sun</i>
<i> look good today? ♪</i>

11:45.029 --> 11:47.537
<i> ♪ Shine ♪</i>

11:47.606 --> 11:50.401
<i>♪ But the rain is on its way ♪</i>

11:52.377 --> 11:54.778
<i> ♪ Shine ♪</i>

11:54.847 --> 11:59.245
<i> ♪ Watch the butcher shine</i>
<i> his knives ♪</i>

11:59.313 --> 12:02.143
Yo, Arj, my Indian brother.
What's going on, man?

12:02.211 --> 12:03.945
Hey, what's up, Leonard?

12:04.014 --> 12:06.280
You know, you don't have
to mention I'm Indian
every time you say hi.

12:06.349 --> 12:08.259
Oh, my bad.
You Pakistani?

12:08.327 --> 12:10.153
Just forget about it.

12:10.222 --> 12:12.423
-Uh, you good?
-Yo, quick favor.

12:12.491 --> 12:14.989
You got some toothpaste
I could borrow? I'm all out.

12:15.058 --> 12:16.730
ARJ: Uh, yeah.

12:16.799 --> 12:18.499
-Here you go.
-Oh, thanks.

12:18.568 --> 12:20.799
Oh, you don't have the one
with the little whitening
crystals, do you?

12:20.868 --> 12:22.266
I got a big date tonight.

12:22.334 --> 12:24.106
No, sorry. What's up
with this big date?

12:24.175 --> 12:28.241
Oh, yo, this girl Susan,
she works at the CVS
up in Burbank.

12:28.310 --> 12:31.811
I asked, I said,
"Yo, why you smell
like blueberries?"

12:31.880 --> 12:33.307
And now,
we're going on a date.

12:33.376 --> 12:34.751
-That worked?
-Hell, yeah.

12:34.820 --> 12:37.588
Dude, girls love it
when you know smells.

12:37.657 --> 12:39.815
That shows you notice things.
Try it.

12:39.884 --> 12:43.760
Go up to a girl
and be like, "Yo, girl,
you smell like a new car."

12:43.828 --> 12:46.095
'Cause that's
everyone's favorite smell.

12:46.164 --> 12:47.928
Well, why didn't you tell Susan
she smelled like a new car?

12:47.997 --> 12:51.495
'Cause she smelled
like blueberries.

12:51.563 --> 12:53.835
Yep, that makes sense.
I'll see you later, Leonard.

12:53.903 --> 12:55.271
Just give me
the toothpaste tomorrow.

12:55.340 --> 12:56.533
Yo, later, man.

13:02.743 --> 13:03.738
(PHONE CHIMES)

13:09.850 --> 13:11.086
(DOORBELL CHIMING)

13:14.323 --> 13:15.787
<i>(BRIGHTER DAYS - UNDERGROUND</i>
<i>GOODIES MIX</i> PLAYING ON STEREO)

13:15.856 --> 13:17.796
(DOORBELL CHIMING)

13:20.158 --> 13:21.564
<i> ♪ Oh, I need, ooh ♪</i>

13:21.632 --> 13:23.533
<i> ♪ Oh, I need, ooh ♪</i>

13:23.601 --> 13:25.403
<i> ♪ Oh, I need, ooh ♪</i>

13:25.471 --> 13:27.438
<i> ♪ Oh, I need, ooh ♪</i>

13:27.507 --> 13:29.363
<i> ♪ Oh, I need, ooh-ooh ♪</i>

13:29.432 --> 13:31.266
<i> ♪ Oh-oh, I-I need, ooh ♪</i>

13:31.334 --> 13:33.202
<i> ♪ Oh, I need, ooh ♪</i>

13:33.270 --> 13:35.136
<i> ♪ Oh, I need, ooh ♪</i>

13:35.205 --> 13:36.578
<i> ♪ Oh, I need ♪</i>

13:36.647 --> 13:38.949
<i> ♪ Brighter days ♪</i>

13:49.161 --> 13:50.255
Arj?

13:50.323 --> 13:51.826
Uh, yeah. I'm here
to clean out the garage.

13:51.895 --> 13:53.988
Nice, nice.
I'm Jeff. A plej.

13:54.056 --> 13:55.227
Wait.

13:55.296 --> 13:56.928
Were you at There Will Be Buns
the other day?

13:56.996 --> 13:58.331
Yeah, love that place.

13:58.399 --> 14:00.429
-Line's pretty
brutal though, huh?
-I hope so.

14:00.498 --> 14:02.433
I'm an investor,
so we likes a long line.

14:02.502 --> 14:04.371
My buddy, David Haberman,
you know what he does?

14:04.440 --> 14:07.004
He pays a guy to wait in line
for him. You should try that.

14:07.072 --> 14:09.046
Mmm. That's a good idea.

14:09.114 --> 14:11.381
Garage is this way. How long
you been doing TaskSergeant?

14:11.450 --> 14:13.080
Uh, a few months.

14:13.149 --> 14:15.180
Oh, got to say, they've
been a lifesaver for me.

14:15.249 --> 14:17.583
My assistant left
a little while ago.

14:17.651 --> 14:18.751
Whoa.

14:18.820 --> 14:20.391
Is that a real 930?

14:20.459 --> 14:21.883
The Widowmaker, right?

14:21.951 --> 14:24.091
Uh, honestly, I have no idea.
I've never even driven it.

14:24.160 --> 14:26.629
-I can't drive stick.
-What? You got to learn.

14:26.698 --> 14:29.727
I will.
But first, the garage.

14:29.796 --> 14:33.261
So, I need
all this stuff put in these
plastic containers here,

14:33.330 --> 14:36.904
and I'd love it if you could
breathe some new life
into these pool floaties.

14:36.973 --> 14:39.241
I miss this T. rex.
He's my boy.

14:39.310 --> 14:42.209
-I got to head back
to the cold plunge.
-What's that?

14:42.278 --> 14:45.309
It's like a really freezing
cold tub of water,

14:45.378 --> 14:47.081
and I sit in there
for three minutes,

14:47.149 --> 14:49.787
and then I run to my sauna
for 15 minutes,

14:49.855 --> 14:51.879
and then I go back
and forth four times.

14:51.948 --> 14:53.653
It's supposed to be very good
for your circulation.

14:53.722 --> 14:54.755
Does it work?

14:54.824 --> 14:56.123
Honestly, I have no idea.

14:56.192 --> 14:57.986
Uh, if you need me,
just knock on the sauna.

14:58.055 --> 14:59.628
All right.

14:59.696 --> 15:01.061
Okay, let's get cold.

15:01.130 --> 15:02.463
<i> (IT'S MY LIFE</i>
BY DA POSSE PLAYING)

15:02.532 --> 15:04.300
(SCREAMS)

15:04.368 --> 15:05.365
Fuck!

15:08.839 --> 15:09.833
-(TIMER BEEPING)
-Oh, thank God.

15:09.902 --> 15:11.175
(GRUNTING)

15:11.243 --> 15:13.769
(SIGHS)

15:15.912 --> 15:17.281
-(TIMER BEEPING)
-Time to plunge.

15:17.350 --> 15:18.609
(SCREAMING)

15:20.378 --> 15:21.945
-(TIMER BEEPING)
-(GRUNTING)

15:22.014 --> 15:23.187
Oh, come on.

15:23.256 --> 15:25.079
(BLOWING)

15:25.147 --> 15:26.251
Boom.

15:26.320 --> 15:29.285
Holy fuck!
Look how clean my garage is.

15:29.353 --> 15:31.126
-Five stars, man.
-Thanks.

15:31.195 --> 15:33.523
Sorry. I got a bit peckish
while you were in there.

15:33.591 --> 15:36.126
You want some burrata?
You a burrata boy?

15:36.194 --> 15:37.764
Uh, not really familiar.

15:37.833 --> 15:39.135
You're shitting me!

15:39.835 --> 15:41.462
Dude, you got to try it.

15:41.531 --> 15:42.974
-It's the best.
-All right.

15:45.775 --> 15:47.209
-Goddamn!
-Yeah!

15:47.277 --> 15:49.439
-That is some creamy cheese.
-It's good shit, right?

15:49.507 --> 15:51.441
Yeah. I guess
I am a burrata boy.

15:51.510 --> 15:54.311
-Welcome to the club.
-(ARJ CHUCKLES)

15:54.380 --> 15:56.781
All right, man,
thank you. Really.

15:56.849 --> 15:57.888
Yeah.

15:57.956 --> 16:00.959
Um, so are you looking
for an assistant?

16:02.393 --> 16:03.786
I am.

16:04.762 --> 16:06.492
Would you ever consider me?

16:07.558 --> 16:09.161
I mean, we just met,
and, you know,

16:09.230 --> 16:11.332
I got a lot going on
in my life.

16:12.372 --> 16:13.999
Yeah, like what?

16:14.067 --> 16:15.972
My current to-do list?

16:16.041 --> 16:18.401
Uh, fix my pool heater,
get new house slippers,

16:18.470 --> 16:20.341
get a disco floor
for my party,

16:20.409 --> 16:22.671
and find a shaman to take me
on an ayahuasca journey.

16:22.739 --> 16:26.017
It really runs the gamut,
but I can do it.

16:26.950 --> 16:28.745
(CLICKS TONGUE)
You know what?

16:30.248 --> 16:32.148
I really like your vibe.

16:32.216 --> 16:37.259
And I am very digging
this initiative that
you're showing right now.

16:37.327 --> 16:39.188
Why don't we do
a one-week trial,
see how it goes?

16:39.256 --> 16:40.388
-I'm in.
-Nice!

16:40.456 --> 16:42.198
Burrata boys for life!

16:43.294 --> 16:44.328
Well, for one week.

16:44.397 --> 16:46.165
If that goes well,
then for life.

16:46.234 --> 16:47.337
<i> (GOOD LIFE</i>
BY INNER CITY PLAYING)

16:47.406 --> 16:48.436
JEFF: Yo!

16:48.505 --> 16:49.898
Hey.

16:49.967 --> 16:52.942
Ayahuasca, I can get you in
with a shaman named Tammy.

16:53.011 --> 16:54.373
I know it doesn't sound
too shaman-y,

16:54.442 --> 16:56.848
but apparently,
she's George Clooney's shaman.

16:56.916 --> 17:00.117
Ooh, he seems very zen.
Yeah, book Tammy.

17:00.947 --> 17:02.544
All right.

17:02.613 --> 17:04.751
-Jeff is in.
-(KEYBOARD CLACKING)

17:04.820 --> 17:06.123
JEFF: Uh-huh.

17:06.191 --> 17:08.385
No, the non-alcoholic
beverage space is exploding.

17:08.454 --> 17:10.589
Yeah, uh,
that sounds good. Yeah.

17:10.657 --> 17:12.428
Just send me the deck.
I'll check it out tomorrow.

17:12.497 --> 17:14.032
Thank you.

17:14.932 --> 17:17.194
Did you salt
the rim on this?

17:17.263 --> 17:18.600
What are you, a magician?

17:18.669 --> 17:19.860
Uh, disco floor,

17:19.929 --> 17:22.404
I found these
super chill Armenian brothers.

17:22.473 --> 17:24.809
They can do it. They just need
to know how big a space it is.

17:24.877 --> 17:26.407
Uh, it's that
whole room in there.

17:26.475 --> 17:28.737
Oh, whoa. You're having
a disco floor in your house?

17:28.805 --> 17:30.705
Yeah, it's, uh...
My 40th is coming up,

17:30.774 --> 17:32.249
so I'm gonna blow it out
a little bit.

17:32.318 --> 17:34.608
I've been working with this
dance choreographer, Shabier.

17:34.677 --> 17:35.718
He's teaching me
a whole routine

17:35.787 --> 17:37.721
-and everything.
-Nice.

17:37.790 --> 17:39.150
Right, so you go
arm then back.

17:39.219 --> 17:40.582
-Yeah.
-And then one.

17:40.651 --> 17:42.156
Yo, Arj, Arj,
will you film this

17:42.225 --> 17:43.553
in case I want
to watch it back later?

17:43.622 --> 17:44.993
-ARJ: Yep. I got you.
-JEFF: Awesome.

17:45.062 --> 17:46.491
-Okay. From arms.
-SHABIER: Ready?

17:46.560 --> 17:49.392
Yeah, from arms, you go,
you, everybody, in,

17:49.461 --> 17:52.494
-love!
-Yeah! That was awesome!

17:52.563 --> 17:53.627
-You got that?
-Yeah, yeah.

17:53.696 --> 17:56.439
My friends are
gonna freak out.

17:56.508 --> 17:58.676
I know you've been looking
for something special
for your 40th.

17:58.744 --> 17:59.976
I think
I found the watch.

18:00.045 --> 18:01.505
Check out
this case-back engraving.

18:01.573 --> 18:03.781
JEFF: Oh, "Pretty Baby."
I love that.

18:03.850 --> 18:06.483
-How much is Pretty Baby?
-$250K.

18:06.552 --> 18:07.810
Let's do it.

18:07.879 --> 18:10.011
Jeff, pool guy can come
fix the heater next week.

18:10.722 --> 18:12.652
Perfect. (CHUCKLES)

18:12.720 --> 18:15.254
So, besides that, you just
have that Zoom in ten minutes.

18:15.323 --> 18:17.419
Oh, great.
Um, two things for you.

18:17.488 --> 18:18.688
You got a parking ticket.

18:18.757 --> 18:20.865
-I put it downstairs
in the kitchen.
-Ugh.

18:20.934 --> 18:23.263
And I got you
a company credit card

18:23.331 --> 18:25.197
for, you know,
expenses and stuff.

18:25.265 --> 18:27.670
ARJ: Whoa. "Sauna Boss LLC."

18:27.739 --> 18:29.202
The one and only.

18:29.271 --> 18:30.465
-Can I ask you something?
-Yeah.

18:30.533 --> 18:32.038
What the fuck do you do?

18:32.106 --> 18:34.978
Oh. Um, I run a VC firm.

18:35.047 --> 18:36.673
Uh, we invest
in smaller companies,

18:36.742 --> 18:38.375
I serve on the board
and consult for them.

18:38.444 --> 18:39.948
Foodzr,
that food delivery app,

18:40.016 --> 18:41.216
-that's one of ours.
-Ah.

18:41.285 --> 18:43.019
Uh, those, like, kiosks
you see at the airport

18:43.088 --> 18:44.613
that sell headphones,
those are ours.

18:44.682 --> 18:45.989
We make a shit ton
off of those.

18:46.058 --> 18:47.721
Nice. And how did
you get into that?

18:47.790 --> 18:49.724
Me and my friends,
we started this thing
with cell phone towers,

18:49.793 --> 18:51.162
that did well.

18:51.230 --> 18:52.520
We took that money,
we put it into this tech thing,

18:52.588 --> 18:53.689
that did really well.

18:53.758 --> 18:57.399
-And now, here we are.
-Here we are.

19:15.049 --> 19:16.451
(ARJ SIGHS)

19:19.318 --> 19:20.752
(PHONE VIBRATING)

19:25.830 --> 19:27.054
Hey, how's it going?

19:27.123 --> 19:28.895
I was about to head over
to pick you up. All good?

19:28.964 --> 19:30.199
ELENA:<i> Hey.</i>

19:30.268 --> 19:32.068
<i> Look, I'm not one to flake,</i>
<i> but I was...</i>

19:32.136 --> 19:33.697
<i> I was driving</i>
<i> my cousin's car,</i>

19:33.766 --> 19:35.201
<i> and I was trying</i>
<i> to send somebody a video</i>

19:35.270 --> 19:36.864
<i> of this dog doing backflips,</i>

19:36.933 --> 19:39.167
<i> and I backed</i>
<i> into a telephone pole.</i>

19:39.236 --> 19:41.910
<i> I'm totally fine, but I should</i>
<i> probably deal with this.</i>

19:41.978 --> 19:43.377
Oh, no, I'm so sorry.

19:43.446 --> 19:46.576
That sounds really annoying
and kinda cute.

19:46.645 --> 19:48.549
Be careful
texting and driving.

19:48.618 --> 19:50.746
<i> I will. Is there any way</i>
<i> we could do another day?</i>

19:50.815 --> 19:53.716
<i> -Like, tomorrow even?</i>
-Of course.

19:53.785 --> 19:56.591
<i> Okay. See you</i>
<i> tomorrow then. Bye.</i>

19:56.660 --> 19:57.657
Bye.

19:59.930 --> 20:01.197
(BELL DINGING SOFTLY)

20:01.266 --> 20:03.563
WOMAN ON APP:
<i> Your session is complete.</i>

20:03.632 --> 20:06.199
<i> See if you can bring</i>
<i> some of this mindfulness</i>

20:06.267 --> 20:07.865
<i> into the rest of your day.</i>

20:09.040 --> 20:12.067
(EXHALES DEEPLY)
Meditation over!

20:13.476 --> 20:15.241
Did you finish unpacking
all those clothes I got?

20:15.310 --> 20:17.077
Yeah, almost.
Love this guy.

20:17.145 --> 20:18.473
Yeah, that's fresh, huh?

20:18.541 --> 20:20.414
-Yeah.
-So...

20:20.483 --> 20:22.211
let me show you something
real quick, okay?

20:22.279 --> 20:23.619
Sure.

20:23.687 --> 20:25.087
So...

20:25.156 --> 20:27.750
God forbid,
any shit goes down,

20:27.819 --> 20:30.525
just want you to know
I have a gun.

20:31.888 --> 20:33.293
It's in this drawer
right here.

20:33.362 --> 20:36.896
Here's the safe.
The code is 1244.

20:36.964 --> 20:38.296
Whoa.

20:38.364 --> 20:39.663
I'm not a big gun guy.

20:39.732 --> 20:41.137
I'll probably just hide,
if that's okay.

20:41.205 --> 20:42.470
Hey, I'm not
a big gun guy, either,

20:42.539 --> 20:43.931
but there was, like,
a bunch of home invasions

20:44.000 --> 20:45.833
in the neighborhood
and I got spooked.

20:45.902 --> 20:47.572
So, Maurice,
he's my gun trainer,

20:47.640 --> 20:49.476
he says if someone's
in your home,

20:49.545 --> 20:52.248
the most important thing is
do not hesitate.

20:52.317 --> 20:54.318
You shoot first,
and you ask questions later.

20:54.387 --> 20:56.947
They could be on meth
or something, you don't know.

20:57.923 --> 20:59.650
Troubling times, my friend.

20:59.718 --> 21:02.326
Oh, also, I need you
to call Dunsmoor

21:02.395 --> 21:04.621
and make me
a dinner reservation
for Friday night.

21:04.690 --> 21:06.426
Just tell Mattias
I'm coming in.

21:06.495 --> 21:09.457
He'll give me a nice table
at the bar.

21:09.526 --> 21:10.667
ARJ: Um, sure.

21:10.736 --> 21:11.927
Oh, by the way,

21:11.996 --> 21:13.632
I was gonna ask,
I actually got a date tonight,

21:13.700 --> 21:15.432
is it all right
if I head out after this?

21:15.501 --> 21:17.707
Yeah. You got a hot date?

21:17.776 --> 21:18.967
What's the plan?

21:19.036 --> 21:21.804
Uh, something low-key.
Probably go get tacos.

21:21.873 --> 21:25.974
Tacos? What?
Do you not like this girl?

21:26.043 --> 21:28.710
Yeah, I like this girl.
Do you not like tacos?

21:28.779 --> 21:30.317
How did you guys
meet each other?

21:30.386 --> 21:32.153
Mmm, we kinda met
at a taco place.

21:32.222 --> 21:34.221
And you're going
for more tacos?

21:34.289 --> 21:36.026
That's too many tacos, man.

21:36.095 --> 21:38.227
That's
an all-taco relationship.

21:38.296 --> 21:40.789
-It's a lot.
-Yeah. Yo, go to Dunsmoor.

21:40.858 --> 21:42.223
That's nice.
She'll like that.

21:42.291 --> 21:45.202
-It's not too pricey, is it?
-No, no, no, not at all.

21:45.271 --> 21:47.368
And make sure you get
the ribeye, it's great.

21:47.436 --> 21:50.207
So let's talk
about the ensemble.

21:50.276 --> 21:52.404
Is this what we're, uh,
wearing on our date?

21:52.473 --> 21:53.938
The coffee stain
and all that?

21:54.778 --> 21:55.940
I guess.

21:57.047 --> 21:58.640
My little jacket.

21:58.709 --> 22:00.075
I got this little jacket.

22:00.144 --> 22:02.018
I bought it a while ago,
and I haven't returned it.

22:02.086 --> 22:03.745
It's a little teensy on me,

22:03.814 --> 22:05.386
but it could be
perfect on you.

22:05.455 --> 22:07.019
Yeah, you can borrow it
for the date.

22:07.088 --> 22:08.089
All right.

22:08.158 --> 22:09.924
-Yeah.
-Ooh, it's nice!

22:09.993 --> 22:11.127
Like a glove.

22:11.196 --> 22:13.128
I feel like Kevin James
in<i> Hitch.</i>

22:13.197 --> 22:15.659
That makes me Hitch in<i> Hitch.</i>

22:15.728 --> 22:17.760
Hah. He's a cool guy.
Thank you.

22:17.829 --> 22:20.235
-I like your jacket.
-Oh, thanks.

22:20.304 --> 22:22.071
-You look very nice, too.
-Thanks.

22:22.140 --> 22:23.730
Um, I'm so glad
we did this.

22:23.799 --> 22:26.372
-Me, too.
-Yeah.

22:26.441 --> 22:27.835
At first,
I kinda hated you.

22:27.904 --> 22:29.342
-What? What did I do?
-Yeah.

22:29.411 --> 22:30.544
I mean, you were
just so, like,

22:30.613 --> 22:31.947
(IN A DRAB VOICE)
"I don't believe in much."

22:32.016 --> 22:33.349
I... Oh, come on.

22:33.417 --> 22:34.943
-I didn't talk like that.
-Yeah. You did.

22:35.012 --> 22:36.209
(IN A DRAB VOICE)
"Oh, I don't know."

22:36.278 --> 22:38.713
-No. Come on.
-You did. Yeah, that was you.

22:38.781 --> 22:40.123
And now, look at you.

22:40.192 --> 22:41.257
Hey, guys,
how are we tonight?

22:41.326 --> 22:43.217
-Hey, how are you?
-Good, thank you.

22:43.286 --> 22:44.891
Thank you. So what are we
thinking food-wise?

22:44.959 --> 22:46.887
ARJ: My friend said
we definitely have
to get a ribeye.

22:46.956 --> 22:48.360
ELENA: It does
look very good.

22:48.429 --> 22:49.630
Oh, it's a signature dish.

22:49.699 --> 22:50.791
They grill it right
on the fire. It's so good.

22:50.860 --> 22:52.264
-ARJ: All right.
-Cool.

22:52.332 --> 22:54.234
-Cool.
-Thanks.

22:54.302 --> 22:57.133
-So we usually say about three
to four plates per person.
-ELENA: All right.

22:57.201 --> 22:58.900
WAITRESS:
Everything is shared,
family style.

22:58.969 --> 23:00.707
And we have
some amazing wines,

23:00.776 --> 23:02.440
if you want to talk
to our sommelier about it.

23:02.509 --> 23:03.708
-Okay.
-WAITRESS: Cool.

23:03.777 --> 23:05.077
-I'll give you guys a minute.
-Thanks.

23:05.145 --> 23:06.578
Welcome.

23:06.647 --> 23:09.220
I am so good
without the ribeye.

23:09.288 --> 23:11.647
-Yeah, it's a big steak.
-(ELENA CHUCKLES)

23:11.715 --> 23:12.748
Maybe we do the trout.

23:12.817 --> 23:14.715
-Trout sounds perfect.
-Yeah.

23:14.783 --> 23:17.128
I'm actually super easy,
and they said everything's
meant to be shared.

23:17.196 --> 23:18.555
-So let's share.
-Yeah. Let's share,

23:18.624 --> 23:20.055
-family style.
-Yeah.

23:20.123 --> 23:21.324
It's a small family,
just the two of us.

23:21.392 --> 23:23.094
No kids.

23:23.163 --> 23:25.431
I'm telling you,
I used to kill it in
my school talent shows.

23:25.500 --> 23:26.928
Really?
What was your talent?

23:26.997 --> 23:29.270
Singing, dancing,
everything.

23:29.339 --> 23:31.639
-Oh. What'd you sing?
-Mmm.

23:31.708 --> 23:33.306
Hey, team. Here's the bill
whenever you're ready.

23:33.375 --> 23:35.072
-Thanks.
-You're welcome.

23:37.174 --> 23:38.443
ELENA: Wow. We should
definitely split this.

23:38.511 --> 23:40.480
No, no, no. I'll get it.

23:40.549 --> 23:42.746
-ELENA: You sure?
-Yeah, yeah.

23:42.815 --> 23:45.254
Don't worry about it.
My treat.

23:45.323 --> 23:47.682
ELENA: Thank you.
This was...

23:47.751 --> 23:48.789
This was so lovely.

24:13.413 --> 24:14.584
JEFF: Hey, Arj?

24:15.548 --> 24:17.287
Hey. You get my email?

24:17.356 --> 24:19.680
Are you all set
for ayahuasca tonight?

24:19.749 --> 24:21.217
Yeah. Um...

24:23.223 --> 24:27.122
Did you use my card
to buy yourself dinner
last night?

24:27.191 --> 24:28.992
I... I talked to your
accountant about that.

24:29.060 --> 24:30.566
I... I'm gonna pay you back
right away.

24:30.635 --> 24:32.966
I just got in a little bit
of a jam at Dunsmoor,

24:33.034 --> 24:34.730
and the waitress recommended
an expensive bottle of wine.

24:34.799 --> 24:35.900
I didn't know what to do.

24:35.968 --> 24:38.206
-You can't do that.
-I totally get that.

24:38.274 --> 24:39.706
It won't happen again.

24:39.775 --> 24:41.373
And I'm gonna pay you back
as soon as I can.

24:41.442 --> 24:43.174
I'm really sorry.

24:43.242 --> 24:46.077
Um, we need to stop
working together,
unfortunately.

24:48.217 --> 24:50.716
-Really?
-Yeah.

24:50.785 --> 24:52.049
I mean, I'm gonna
pay you back, man.

24:52.118 --> 24:54.521
You told me to go there.
You said it wasn't pricey.

24:54.590 --> 24:56.417
Just don't
make it weird, okay?

24:56.486 --> 24:59.024
Just, thank you for everything,
and I'm really sorry.

25:00.956 --> 25:02.291
Um, I'm sorry, too.

25:15.014 --> 25:17.044
"Currently full"?

25:17.112 --> 25:18.109
(SIGHS)

25:25.151 --> 25:26.723
-WOMAN: Have you
done this before?
-ARJ: No.

25:26.792 --> 25:29.887
Whole process takes
about an hour and a half
to two hours.

25:29.956 --> 25:31.086
TAMMY: Tonight,
we're gonna be working

25:31.154 --> 25:34.959
with magic mushrooms
and ayahuasca.

25:35.028 --> 25:36.633
All right, the needle's
gonna go right here.

25:48.375 --> 25:50.339
(RETCHING)

25:52.048 --> 25:53.144
(GROANS)

25:56.151 --> 25:57.249
(LAUGHS)

25:57.318 --> 25:59.018
(RETCHING)

25:59.815 --> 26:01.823
(PANTING)

26:10.792 --> 26:11.926
MAN: Yo.

26:11.994 --> 26:13.602
Get your lil' ass up.

26:13.671 --> 26:15.999
You can't be sleeping
in no Denny's, man.

26:16.068 --> 26:17.408
-I'm sorry.
-And them outlets are off.

26:17.476 --> 26:19.335
You ain't getting no juice
to your phone.

26:27.886 --> 26:29.517
Hey!

26:29.586 --> 26:31.686
Did you see a Golf
parked out here?

26:31.754 --> 26:33.618
The one with the duct tape
on the bumper?

26:33.687 --> 26:35.620
-Yeah.
-It got towed.

26:35.689 --> 26:37.620
Towed? Why'd it get towed?

26:37.689 --> 26:39.124
I don't know.

26:39.193 --> 26:41.832
Am I dressed like a cop
or a guy that works at Denny's?

26:41.900 --> 26:42.897
Denny's.

26:44.496 --> 26:45.628
(SIGHS)

26:45.697 --> 26:46.934
Parking tickets.

26:48.064 --> 26:49.871
MAN: Yeah, that'll do it.

26:49.940 --> 26:51.699
They gonna charge you for
the tickets and for the tow.

26:51.768 --> 26:53.169
I'm sorry.

26:53.237 --> 26:54.510
If I knew your night
was going like this,

26:54.579 --> 26:56.141
I'd have let you sleep
some more, man.

27:04.747 --> 27:06.217
(SIGHS)

27:16.894 --> 27:18.801
His head's in his hands.

27:20.236 --> 27:21.397
I knew it.

27:22.965 --> 27:25.500
A lost soul.

27:27.909 --> 27:30.873
Arj, I'm an angel.
My name is Gabriel.

27:30.941 --> 27:32.177
I'm here to save you.

27:33.578 --> 27:34.749
What?

27:34.818 --> 27:36.852
Who the fuck are you?
How do you know my name?

27:38.884 --> 27:40.386
Maybe you don't understand.

27:40.455 --> 27:42.718
I'm an angel.

27:42.787 --> 27:45.023
See the wings?

27:45.092 --> 27:47.430
I've been observing you.
I know all about you.

27:47.499 --> 27:49.499
I know you're living
in your car.

27:49.567 --> 27:51.831
I know you lost
your job with Jeff.

27:51.899 --> 27:54.162
-What?
-I even know that right now

27:54.231 --> 27:55.229
there's a part
of you that thinks

27:55.298 --> 27:56.898
your life
isn't worth living.

27:56.967 --> 27:58.902
But it's not true.

27:58.971 --> 28:01.539
You have so much
to live for.

28:01.608 --> 28:03.142
Let me show you.

28:06.109 --> 28:08.582
Holy shit!
What happened?

28:08.651 --> 28:10.050
What is this?
Where are we?

28:10.118 --> 28:14.254
Visions that reflect the hope
your life promises.

28:14.323 --> 28:18.520
I know you've been having
trouble finding work now,
but look.

28:21.459 --> 28:24.058
I get a job driving one
of those delivery trucks?

28:24.127 --> 28:25.865
-Yes.
-MAN: Hey, Arj.

28:25.933 --> 28:27.463
Don't forget
your pee bottle, bro.

28:28.803 --> 28:30.538
Why do I need
a pee bottle?

28:30.607 --> 28:32.103
Your deadlines
are very strict

28:32.172 --> 28:34.376
and you don't have time
for bathroom breaks.

28:34.444 --> 28:36.340
Hence the pee bottle.

28:37.983 --> 28:38.974
Okay.

28:39.042 --> 28:41.246
But wait, there's more.

28:44.724 --> 28:48.491
I know you're living
in your car now, but look.

28:48.560 --> 28:50.584
Elena and I
move in together?

28:50.653 --> 28:53.125
Um, technically, you both
move in with her mom.

28:53.194 --> 28:55.764
Elena, Darryl and Mercedes
are coming over again.

28:55.833 --> 28:57.767
So could you two sleep
in the living room?

28:57.836 --> 28:59.300
And fold the couch bed up
in the morning, please.

28:59.369 --> 29:00.661
Yes, yes, Ma.

29:00.729 --> 29:03.071
Hey, has anyone seen
my air fryer? I can't find it.

29:03.139 --> 29:05.940
For the millionth time, Jay,
I didn't use your air fryer.

29:06.009 --> 29:07.736
I'm just eating spaghetti,
minding my business.

29:07.804 --> 29:09.178
Fuck it.

29:09.247 --> 29:10.804
Who's that guy?

29:10.873 --> 29:13.978
It's her sister
Patrice's on-and-off-again
boyfriend, Jay.

29:14.047 --> 29:16.113
-They live here, too.
-JAY: Arj,

29:16.181 --> 29:17.453
have you been
using my body wash?

29:17.521 --> 29:18.815
I'm missing some body wash.

29:18.884 --> 29:20.814
Seems a bit crowded.

29:20.883 --> 29:25.895
But you both
eventually get steady jobs
and move to Texas.

29:30.367 --> 29:31.828
FUTURE ARJ: Hey.

29:31.897 --> 29:33.834
So what'd they say?

29:33.902 --> 29:35.965
He's gonna have
to have the surgery.

29:36.033 --> 29:37.603
Okay, how much is it?

29:37.672 --> 29:39.543
We can't afford it.

29:39.612 --> 29:41.435
Then what's gonna
happen to Dapper?

29:41.504 --> 29:42.869
Does that mean
we're gonna have to...

29:42.938 --> 29:44.146
Oh.

29:44.214 --> 29:46.139
Oh, no.

29:46.208 --> 29:48.683
I'm so sorry, buddy.

29:48.752 --> 29:51.449
We have to put
the dog to sleep?

29:51.518 --> 29:53.214
Yes.

29:53.283 --> 29:54.649
Let's maybe
get out of here.

29:56.353 --> 29:58.552
That's what I have
to live for?

29:58.621 --> 30:01.793
Yeah. What's wrong?
Why are you so upset?

30:01.861 --> 30:03.362
Because my life sucks!

30:03.431 --> 30:07.128
I mean, it's not the
worst life in the world,
but damn, man.

30:07.196 --> 30:09.364
Pee bottle? Dead dog?

30:09.433 --> 30:10.736
I did everything
I was supposed to do,

30:10.805 --> 30:12.172
and nothing's working out.

30:13.943 --> 30:16.537
I'm going to be honest
with you, Arj.

30:16.605 --> 30:19.139
I'm not really supposed
to be doing this.

30:19.208 --> 30:20.210
What does that mean?

30:20.279 --> 30:23.687
I'm overstepping
my bounds as an angel.

30:23.755 --> 30:26.181
Do you see how my wings
are kind of small?

30:26.250 --> 30:27.514
I wasn't gonna
say anything,

30:27.583 --> 30:29.524
but yeah,
they're on the tinier side.

30:29.593 --> 30:32.088
It means I'm lower order.

30:32.156 --> 30:33.356
I'm normally only in charge

30:33.424 --> 30:35.866
of saving people
from texting and driving.

30:35.935 --> 30:39.533
Wait. You're telling me I have
a budget guardian angel?

30:39.601 --> 30:42.197
-Kinda.
-(SIGHS)

30:42.266 --> 30:43.934
I'm just trying
to help you.

30:44.002 --> 30:45.732
I want you to have hope.

30:45.801 --> 30:49.346
I need to show you
that your life is precious,

30:49.414 --> 30:51.513
that it's worth living.

30:51.581 --> 30:53.114
My life isn't precious.

30:53.182 --> 30:56.080
My life is just in the service
of people like Jeff,

30:56.149 --> 30:57.578
the people
who actually get to live

30:57.646 --> 31:00.847
and go on vacations
and do cold plunges.

31:00.916 --> 31:04.653
You think Jeff's life is
the life that's worth living?

31:06.027 --> 31:09.093
Maybe I can show you
that that life

31:09.162 --> 31:11.561
is not all
it's cracked up to be.

31:13.834 --> 31:14.828
(TAPPING ON CAR WINDOW)

31:17.936 --> 31:19.074
GUARD: Sir?

31:22.447 --> 31:24.444
Sir, are you okay?

31:24.512 --> 31:26.443
What?

31:26.512 --> 31:28.417
You must've fallen asleep
in your car. (CHUCKLES)

31:28.486 --> 31:31.951
Yeah, I fell asleep.

31:32.020 --> 31:34.454
No problem.
Get home safe, okay?

31:34.522 --> 31:35.926
Okay.

31:41.724 --> 31:43.060
FEMALE AUTOMATED VOICE:
<i> Good morning, Arj.</i>

31:43.128 --> 31:46.062
<i> Would you like to go home?</i>

31:46.130 --> 31:47.465
<i> Navigating to home.</i>

31:47.534 --> 31:51.172
<i> Estimated drive time,</i>
<i> one hour and ten minutes.</i>

32:28.676 --> 32:30.112
ARJ: Jeff?

32:31.283 --> 32:33.039
JEFF: Yo!

32:33.108 --> 32:35.852
I was just upstairs unloading
some packages that came in.

32:35.920 --> 32:37.618
Those house slippers
you wanted arrived.

32:37.687 --> 32:39.121
They're very cool.

32:40.187 --> 32:42.823
-What are you doing?
-Nothing.

32:42.892 --> 32:45.188
You good?
You need anything?

32:45.257 --> 32:48.664
-No, I'm good.
-All right.

32:48.733 --> 32:51.362
Uh, I'm gonna
go finish up.

32:51.431 --> 32:54.466
Just let me know
if you want anything, okay?

32:56.432 --> 32:58.074
-Uh, hey, Jeff.
-Yeah?

33:00.204 --> 33:01.737
Whose house is this?

33:03.207 --> 33:05.411
Your house. (CHUCKLES)

33:25.801 --> 33:27.601
Enjoying your new life?

33:27.670 --> 33:28.929
What's happened?

33:28.998 --> 33:31.706
You wanted to have wealth
and success, here you go.

33:31.774 --> 33:33.042
Take a good look around,

33:33.111 --> 33:35.743
see if Jeff's life is
all it's cracked up to be.

33:35.811 --> 33:36.946
I'll check in on you,

33:37.015 --> 33:38.373
and at the end of the week,
we'll assess.

33:38.441 --> 33:40.344
-But I'm still me?
-Yes.

33:40.413 --> 33:43.017
Your name is Arj,
you look like you,

33:43.085 --> 33:46.249
but everything else
is Jeff's life.

33:46.318 --> 33:49.416
Both the good
and the bad.

33:49.484 --> 33:50.893
What happened to Jeff?

33:50.962 --> 33:53.629
He has your life.
He thinks he's you.

33:53.697 --> 33:55.231
So he's my assistant?

33:55.300 --> 33:56.691
Yes.

33:56.759 --> 33:57.958
So he has to do
whatever I ask him to do?

33:58.666 --> 33:59.693
Yes.

33:59.761 --> 34:01.066
If I'm hungry
and I want a snack?

34:01.135 --> 34:03.130
GABRIEL:
He'll get it for you.

34:03.199 --> 34:04.366
Hey, Jeff!

34:04.435 --> 34:06.870
Chips and guac
coming right up.

34:06.938 --> 34:08.605
My man!

34:08.674 --> 34:09.978
JEFF: I'm just gonna
head upstairs to your room,

34:10.046 --> 34:11.238
and finish unpacking
those clothes.

34:11.307 --> 34:12.614
All right, cool.

34:12.683 --> 34:14.807
Enjoying the pool?

34:14.876 --> 34:17.312
Gabriel, the angel!
Can Jeff see you?

34:17.380 --> 34:18.988
No, only you can see me.

34:19.057 --> 34:22.256
Ah. Well, I got to say,
so far, this is great.

34:22.325 --> 34:23.992
You want to hit the pool?
Pop on some trunks?

34:24.060 --> 34:25.993
Hey, Arj, uh,
just reminding you,

34:26.062 --> 34:27.392
you got this meeting
coming up.

34:27.461 --> 34:29.123
You should probably
get ready to go soon.

34:29.191 --> 34:30.834
Meeting?

34:30.902 --> 34:31.963
I don't know
anything about his work.

34:32.032 --> 34:33.134
What am I gonna say?

34:33.202 --> 34:35.970
You wanted to see
what this life is like.

34:36.039 --> 34:39.269
Time to get to work,
Mr. Mogul.

34:39.338 --> 34:40.668
-That's for you.
-ARJ: Oh, God.

34:40.736 --> 34:42.541
There we go,
bon appe-fucking-tit.

34:46.243 --> 34:47.477
Oh, my God!

34:47.546 --> 34:50.020
-This sushi's insane!
-So sick, right?

34:50.089 --> 34:52.656
They fly the fish in
from Japan every morning.

34:52.724 --> 34:54.283
Very high carbon footprint.

34:54.352 --> 34:55.684
-That's awesome.
-Yeah.

34:55.753 --> 34:57.025
Yo, did you check out
that launch proposal

34:57.093 --> 34:58.189
I sent over
for the event next week?

34:58.258 --> 34:59.360
What'd you think
about that?

34:59.826 --> 35:00.825
Uh...

35:00.893 --> 35:02.258
"Uh..."

35:02.326 --> 35:04.027
Looked good, I guess.

35:04.096 --> 35:06.794
Yeah? Great.

35:06.863 --> 35:08.435
All right. Well, yeah,
that's all the business

35:08.504 --> 35:10.502
we had to get to today.
So, what the fuck? How's life?

35:10.571 --> 35:13.808
Uh, same old. Just working,
cold plunging. You?

35:13.877 --> 35:15.209
Work has been crazy, man.

35:15.278 --> 35:17.143
I had to fire one
of my assistants, Darren.

35:17.212 --> 35:18.476
-Oh.
-Yeah, he's a sweetheart.

35:18.545 --> 35:20.884
But I had this big event
in New York last week

35:20.952 --> 35:22.450
and I put him
in charge of vibes.

35:22.519 --> 35:24.313
And then I get there,
and the vibes are
just super off.

35:24.381 --> 35:25.381
-Hate that.
-Yeah.

35:25.450 --> 35:27.114
-Wrong kind of candles.
-Oh.

35:27.182 --> 35:29.320
He didn't tag
the liquor sponsor
in the media posts.

35:29.389 --> 35:31.193
-No!
-The event was off a cliff.

35:31.262 --> 35:33.053
-The vibes were just tanked.
-What was the scent

35:33.122 --> 35:34.721
he was supposed to get
and what did he grab instead?

35:34.790 --> 35:35.863
He was supposed
to get sandalwood.

35:35.932 --> 35:36.998
-He got vetiver.
-Ugh!

35:37.067 --> 35:38.559
Whole place
smelled like shit.

35:38.628 --> 35:40.060
Those aren't the same smells.

35:40.129 --> 35:41.464
-Everybody at the event
must've been furious.
-Yeah.

35:41.533 --> 35:43.031
But you know
what though, dude?

35:43.100 --> 35:46.209
I've been reading a lot about,
like, empathy and forgiveness

35:46.277 --> 35:48.373
in this new Jay Shetty book,
so blessings to Darren.

35:48.442 --> 35:50.307
Ah, thank you.
Hey, let me get this.

35:50.376 --> 35:52.741
Dude, no. Put it
on the company.

35:52.810 --> 35:54.841
It was a "business lunch"
after all, right?

35:54.910 --> 35:57.184
(LAUGHS) Oh, yeah.
Why would we pay?

35:57.253 --> 36:00.189
This was the best lunch
I've ever had!

36:00.258 --> 36:02.192
MAN: Thank you. All right,
we got to go, though.

36:02.261 --> 36:04.391
I got to hit the cardio store,
get a couple nibbles.

36:04.460 --> 36:06.856
<i> (DO YOU WANNA FUNK</i>
BY PATRICK COWLEY PLAYING)

36:12.066 --> 36:13.165
MAN: Excuse me, sir.

36:13.234 --> 36:14.733
ARJ: Oh, hi.
Can I help you?

36:14.802 --> 36:17.434
Yeah, I'm Grant. You called me
to check out the pool heater.

36:17.503 --> 36:19.272
Ooh, that's right.
What's the deal?

36:19.340 --> 36:20.944
So, bad news,
the heater's busted.

36:21.012 --> 36:22.208
Probably gonna have
to replace it.

36:22.277 --> 36:23.846
Probably like 30K
for the heater,

36:23.915 --> 36:26.009
another five
for the install.

36:26.077 --> 36:27.107
Okay.

36:28.478 --> 36:30.616
Problems with your home?

36:30.685 --> 36:35.024
Some pretty serious expenses.
Must be inconvenient.

36:35.092 --> 36:36.557
Good thing I got
a shit ton of money

36:36.626 --> 36:39.288
to cover any and all problems
that come my way. (CHUCKLES)

36:39.357 --> 36:40.587
See you later, Gabe.

36:40.655 --> 36:42.524
I'm off to the sauna.

36:42.592 --> 36:43.924
<i> ♪ There is something ♪</i>

36:43.992 --> 36:45.795
ARJ: So she doesn't
remember me at all?

36:45.864 --> 36:48.598
This version of you
didn't exist until today.

36:48.667 --> 36:52.172
So you'll have
to reintroduce yourself.

36:52.241 --> 36:54.367
<i> ♪ ...that I want to know ♪</i>

36:54.435 --> 36:55.410
Okay.

36:56.880 --> 36:58.347
Elena from lumber.

36:59.177 --> 37:00.746
Uh, yeah.

37:00.815 --> 37:02.710
You helped me find some lumber
one time. It was very helpful.

37:02.779 --> 37:04.646
Oh, well,
I'm glad it worked out.

37:04.715 --> 37:05.985
ARJ: How's it going
over there?

37:06.054 --> 37:07.048
ELENA: In lumber?

37:08.153 --> 37:09.623
It's good.

37:09.691 --> 37:12.619
I'm glad. I was just over
in plumbing, it's a shit show.

37:12.688 --> 37:14.990
-(CHUCKLES)
-I'm Arj.

37:16.295 --> 37:17.729
Nice to meet you, Arj.

37:17.798 --> 37:20.570
<i> ♪ If you wanna funk,</i>
<i> let me show you how ♪</i>

37:20.639 --> 37:21.729
(INAUDIBLE)

37:21.798 --> 37:24.732
<i>♪ Do you wanna funk with me? ♪</i>

37:24.801 --> 37:26.505
Do we have any thoughts
food-wise?

37:26.574 --> 37:28.605
Uh, I mean, we were
looking at the ribeye.

37:28.674 --> 37:30.775
-It does look very good.
-Let's do it.

37:32.717 --> 37:35.445
(INAUDIBLE)

37:35.513 --> 37:36.809
This wine is drinking great.

37:36.878 --> 37:38.583
And this food
is eating great.

37:38.652 --> 37:41.422
Be careful. You gonna
give me gout tonight.

37:41.491 --> 37:43.651
It has been such a pleasure
serving you guys.

37:43.719 --> 37:45.485
Uh, dinner's on us tonight.

37:45.554 --> 37:46.587
-What?
-No.

37:46.655 --> 37:48.628
-What? What?
-Yes.

37:52.900 --> 37:53.930
Oh, no.

37:55.206 --> 37:57.205
Fascinating couple
of days, I imagine.

37:57.273 --> 37:59.437
Hey, what's up?
You need something?

37:59.506 --> 38:01.536
I'm kinda busy
ordering clothes.

38:01.605 --> 38:03.509
So, what are you thinking?

38:03.578 --> 38:05.579
The week is over,
are you ready to go back?

38:06.412 --> 38:08.010
Go back?
What do you mean?

38:08.079 --> 38:11.819
Don't you see what's special
about your life as it was?

38:11.888 --> 38:16.590
You see how superficial
a life of wealth and success
ultimately is?

38:17.353 --> 38:18.658
No.

38:18.726 --> 38:23.231
But have you really reflected
on your experience?

38:23.300 --> 38:25.332
Are you nuts?
I was living in my car!

38:25.400 --> 38:27.160
Now I'm living
in this giant house.

38:27.229 --> 38:29.172
I can buy whatever I want,
do whatever I want.

38:29.240 --> 38:31.006
But what about your job?
What about Elena?

38:31.074 --> 38:32.174
What about the pool heater?

38:32.243 --> 38:34.533
Who gives a fuck
about the pool heater?

38:34.602 --> 38:37.643
I show you something
to make you realize
your life is precious.

38:37.712 --> 38:40.415
You see it and you go back.
You can't just stay.

38:40.484 --> 38:43.452
So it's all over?
You're gonna make me go back?

38:44.251 --> 38:45.421
No, I can't do that.

38:46.455 --> 38:48.256
So if I want to stay,
I can just stay?

38:48.324 --> 38:49.753
-Yes.
-I have to want to go back?

38:49.822 --> 38:51.190
-That's right.
-Then I don't want to go back.

38:51.258 --> 38:52.426
But you can't do that!

38:52.495 --> 38:55.094
-You just said I could.
-(GRUMBLES) Shucks.

38:55.163 --> 38:56.764
You guided someone?

38:56.833 --> 39:01.435
Gabriel, you're not
supposed to talk to people
or be visible.

39:01.503 --> 39:04.268
-I know that.
-Then why did you do this?

39:04.337 --> 39:05.874
He was a lost soul.

39:05.943 --> 39:07.100
I tried to show him

39:07.169 --> 39:09.677
that wealth wouldn't
solve all his problems.

39:09.746 --> 39:10.939
And?

39:11.008 --> 39:14.514
It seems to have solved
most of his problems.

39:14.582 --> 39:17.682
Gabriel, you were
supposed to help Elena.

39:17.751 --> 39:20.420
What you've done has
really changed things.

39:20.489 --> 39:22.421
She had to cancel
her date with Arj

39:22.490 --> 39:24.293
and that set off
a chain reaction.

39:24.362 --> 39:26.920
The date went differently,
Arj lost his job,

39:26.989 --> 39:28.394
and that's
what's led us here.

39:28.463 --> 39:30.893
You have to get Arj
to go back.

39:30.962 --> 39:34.571
And until you do,
I have to take your wings.

39:34.639 --> 39:36.464
Oh, man.

39:36.533 --> 39:38.474
Turn around.

39:42.638 --> 39:43.974
(MARTHA SIGHS)

39:45.975 --> 39:48.115
<i> (PUSH IT</i>
BY SALT-N-PEPA PLAYING)

39:48.183 --> 39:49.751
<i> ♪ Ow! Baby! ♪</i>

39:49.819 --> 39:51.245
My guy!

39:52.223 --> 39:55.887
Hey! Who wants
some fresh bubble?

39:56.551 --> 39:58.620
Whoa!

39:58.688 --> 40:01.656
Justin needs them bubs.

40:01.724 --> 40:04.760
Elena needs some bubs.

40:04.829 --> 40:06.464
Tell me what you think.
Be honest.

40:06.533 --> 40:08.504
Don't lie to me,
don't lie to me.

40:09.402 --> 40:10.996
How's it drinking?

40:11.065 --> 40:12.937
-That's drinking nice.
-Yes.

40:14.374 --> 40:15.970
Jeff! Come here, man.

40:16.038 --> 40:18.073
Have some wine.
Have a little glass.

40:18.142 --> 40:20.582
-Oh, wow. Thanks.
-Here, have some. Have fun.

40:23.088 --> 40:25.420
-That's really good.
-Yeah.

40:25.488 --> 40:26.947
I should get back
to cleaning up, though.

40:27.016 --> 40:28.920
Good call.
Keep cleaning, Jeff.

40:29.661 --> 40:31.189
Hey!

40:31.258 --> 40:33.192
It's Gabriel!

40:33.261 --> 40:35.188
Gabriel, the angel.

40:35.257 --> 40:37.330
-Where's your little wings?
-I lost them.

40:37.398 --> 40:38.695
Ooh. You've been a bad boy.

40:38.764 --> 40:40.500
So no wings,
what does that mean?

40:40.569 --> 40:42.368
People can see me,
I have less powers.

40:42.437 --> 40:44.504
-It's very embarrassing.
-Uh-oh.

40:44.572 --> 40:47.471
Listen, I know
you like this life,

40:47.540 --> 40:49.473
but may I pose a question?

40:49.541 --> 40:51.178
Is this fair to Jeff?

40:51.246 --> 40:53.342
Jeff? Jeff's chilling.

40:53.410 --> 40:54.550
Is he?

40:56.251 --> 40:57.245
ARJ: What are you doing?

41:05.295 --> 41:07.728
Why am I holding
my own trash?

41:08.924 --> 41:10.060
Why are you in my clothes?

41:11.795 --> 41:13.134
What's happening right now?

41:13.202 --> 41:14.669
What did you do to me?

41:15.600 --> 41:17.639
(HYPERVENTILATING)

41:19.539 --> 41:21.209
-Oh, no.
-What happened?

41:21.277 --> 41:22.477
I gave him his memory back,

41:22.545 --> 41:24.044
but I think he may
have went into shock.

41:24.113 --> 41:25.178
Is he dead?

41:25.247 --> 41:27.150
No. Definitely not.

41:27.219 --> 41:29.709
Oh, shit,
some dude just died.

41:29.778 --> 41:30.985
Let's bounce.

41:31.054 --> 41:32.588
He's not dead!

41:33.617 --> 41:36.253
I hope not.

41:36.321 --> 41:40.024
I did not know you were
struggling to the point
that you needed

41:40.922 --> 41:43.056
divine intervention.

41:43.125 --> 41:44.726
But you got
to switch back, man!

41:44.794 --> 41:46.732
Give me my life back.

41:46.801 --> 41:48.899
So, what? I just go back
to living in my car?

41:48.967 --> 41:51.406
-You lived in your car?
-Yes, Jeff, I did.

41:51.475 --> 41:53.033
Why do you think
an angel got involved?

41:53.102 --> 41:54.405
'Cause I had
too many roommates?

41:54.474 --> 41:56.342
Okay, that's bad.

41:56.410 --> 41:58.005
And I acknowledge that.

41:58.074 --> 41:59.907
So here's
what I'm going to do.

41:59.976 --> 42:01.712
If you switch back
right now,

42:01.781 --> 42:04.852
I'm going
to give you $200,000.

42:04.921 --> 42:07.114
(SNICKERS) You spend more than
that on one of your watches!

42:07.183 --> 42:08.387
You're lowballing me
on your existence?

42:08.455 --> 42:09.457
You live in your car!

42:09.525 --> 42:10.591
I thought that'd be
a lot to you.

42:10.659 --> 42:12.119
-I don't know.
-How greedy are you, man?

42:12.188 --> 42:13.762
I'm not greedy!
It's an opening offer!

42:13.831 --> 42:15.295
-That's how negotiations work.
-That's worth your entire life?

42:15.364 --> 42:16.932
Counter! Make me an offer.

42:17.001 --> 42:18.859
Time out, guys.

42:18.927 --> 42:21.026
You can't do that, Jeff.

42:21.095 --> 42:22.603
This is Arj's experience.

42:22.672 --> 42:25.271
-You might not
remember anything.
-What?

42:25.340 --> 42:26.769
Okay, how's this?

42:26.838 --> 42:29.578
Switch back,
or you are evil,

42:29.647 --> 42:32.375
and this angel man will
send you to Hell forever.

42:32.444 --> 42:33.479
Smite him!

42:33.548 --> 42:35.108
I can't send someone to Hell.

42:35.177 --> 42:36.484
That's actually
not my department.

42:36.553 --> 42:39.380
Good God, man,
you are very unhelpful!

42:41.221 --> 42:42.251
Listen.

42:43.160 --> 42:45.152
I drive around L.A.

42:45.220 --> 42:49.593
I see the homeless,
houseless crisis

42:49.661 --> 42:50.895
that has befallen us,

42:50.964 --> 42:52.960
and I did not know that
you were a part of that,

42:53.028 --> 42:54.267
and I don't want you to be.

42:54.336 --> 42:55.831
But that being said,

42:55.900 --> 42:58.503
I think stealing
my entire life

42:58.571 --> 42:59.939
is a little bit harsh.

43:01.402 --> 43:03.108
GABRIEL: You're not
a bad person, Arj.

43:03.176 --> 43:06.374
I know you don't
want to hurt Jeff
to have a good life.

43:08.312 --> 43:10.517
-All right, I'll switch back.
-Yeah! Fuck yeah!

43:10.586 --> 43:12.781
-But I want a few days.
-For what?

43:12.850 --> 43:14.089
To do some fun shit, okay?

43:14.158 --> 43:16.450
Come on, a few days.

43:17.928 --> 43:18.925
Jeff?

43:21.725 --> 43:23.094
You know what?

43:23.162 --> 43:26.097
If that's what
you feel you need,
I will do that.

43:27.401 --> 43:28.662
-Okay.
-Okay.

43:28.730 --> 43:31.265
Okay.

43:31.334 --> 43:32.673
So in the meantime,
can I get a few grand

43:32.742 --> 43:34.668
so I can get, like,
a hotel room and shit?

43:34.737 --> 43:36.706
Yeah, yeah,
let's get you a nice suite
at the Chateau Marmont.

43:36.774 --> 43:38.374
Or how about get fucked!

43:38.443 --> 43:41.143
You fired me
'cause I put, like, $300
on your credit card!

43:41.211 --> 43:43.246
Why don't you tough it out
for a few days?

43:44.520 --> 43:46.221
I see
what's happening here.

43:46.290 --> 43:47.950
Eat the rich, am I right?

43:48.019 --> 43:49.448
You think
'cause I'm a tech bro,

43:49.517 --> 43:51.558
I can't live your life
for a little while?

43:51.627 --> 43:53.693
I can live your life
in my sleep.

43:53.761 --> 43:55.956
I came from nothing.
I'm self-made.

43:56.024 --> 43:57.291
You came from nothing?

43:57.360 --> 43:59.828
Oh, I came from very,
very humble beginnings.

43:59.896 --> 44:00.898
What'd your parents do?

44:00.967 --> 44:03.734
My father was
an orthopedic surgeon,

44:03.803 --> 44:06.473
and my mother
practiced law.

44:06.542 --> 44:08.207
-Hmm.
-At a pretty big firm.

44:08.276 --> 44:09.379
ARJ: Hmm.

44:09.447 --> 44:11.006
But that is not
the money that I got

44:11.075 --> 44:12.479
for my cell phone
tower thing.

44:12.548 --> 44:13.980
That came from
my grandfather,

44:15.285 --> 44:16.653
who owned newspapers.

44:18.221 --> 44:19.684
You know what?

44:19.753 --> 44:23.050
Enjoy the fruits
of my hard work.

44:23.119 --> 44:25.994
I'll be out there
just fine!

44:26.062 --> 44:27.191
Okay.

44:30.093 --> 44:31.499
Well, what are
you going to do?

44:31.568 --> 44:33.500
I'm going to give you
some space

44:33.569 --> 44:35.695
and see you
in a few days.

44:35.764 --> 44:36.772
Bye.

44:38.240 --> 44:40.006
Hey, Jeff?

44:40.075 --> 44:43.839
So, um, since I lost my wings,
I need a place to stay.

44:43.907 --> 44:45.274
Can I move in with you?

44:45.343 --> 44:48.340
I mean, I'm living in this
yucky little motel now.

44:48.409 --> 44:50.552
What, are we going
to share a bed?

44:50.621 --> 44:53.719
I'll go under the covers
and you go over.

44:53.788 --> 44:55.282
Or I'll go over
and you go under.

44:55.351 --> 44:57.991
Whichever you prefer.
What do you say?

44:59.128 --> 45:00.158
Roomies?

45:04.763 --> 45:06.032
I'll be right down.

45:09.131 --> 45:12.071
So, like,
could you fly?

45:13.373 --> 45:15.409
Uh, no.

45:15.477 --> 45:17.942
My wings were too small.

45:18.011 --> 45:20.615
Well, it's not
the size of the wing.

45:20.684 --> 45:23.577
-Actually, it is.
-Oh, that's too bad.

45:27.555 --> 45:28.549
(KNOCKING AT DOOR)

45:29.490 --> 45:30.485
WOMAN: Hello?

45:32.697 --> 45:34.425
-(KNOCKING AT DOOR)
-WOMAN: Checkout time.

45:34.493 --> 45:35.927
Hello?

45:35.995 --> 45:37.462
-(KNOCKING AT DOOR)
-WOMAN: Hello?

45:37.531 --> 45:38.526
One second.

45:41.403 --> 45:42.398
WOMAN: Hello?

45:45.870 --> 45:47.271
(KNOCKING AT DOOR)

45:48.906 --> 45:50.813
Uh, checkout time.

45:50.882 --> 45:54.109
I don't want to check out.
I would like to stay here.

45:54.178 --> 45:56.076
You want to stay,
you pay money.

45:56.145 --> 45:59.247
-How much money?
-$125.

45:59.316 --> 46:01.455
I don't have
that much money right now.

46:01.524 --> 46:03.484
If no have, you check out.

46:03.553 --> 46:06.554
How about I pay you
by tonight? Is that okay?

46:07.727 --> 46:08.963
-Okay.
-Thank you.

46:12.165 --> 46:13.935
We need to find a way
to make some money.

46:14.733 --> 46:16.773
(HORN BLARING)

46:18.342 --> 46:19.799
WOMAN: Here you go.

46:19.868 --> 46:22.476
Hey, is there any update
on the huevos rancheros
for Alex?

46:22.544 --> 46:24.271
Um, gonna be another 15.

46:24.340 --> 46:25.639
-Fifteen minutes?
-(HORN BLARING)

46:25.707 --> 46:27.506
-I don't know, man.
-I'm double parked over here!

46:27.575 --> 46:28.779
-You hear these honks?
-(HORN BLARING)

46:28.847 --> 46:29.844
These honks are for me!

46:29.913 --> 46:31.180
Order for Alex.

46:31.249 --> 46:32.951
Thank you. What happened
to 15 minutes?

46:33.019 --> 46:34.017
WOMAN: What do
you want me to say?

46:34.086 --> 46:35.385
-I hate my life.
-JEFF: Thank you.

46:35.453 --> 46:38.023
WOMAN 2: Come on! You can't
double park! Let's go!

46:38.092 --> 46:40.025
-One second.
-WOMAN 2: Get a pet-sitting job!

46:40.094 --> 46:41.724
-Sorry! Okay.
-WOMAN 2: Let's go, go, go!

46:41.793 --> 46:43.561
Oh, my God.

46:43.630 --> 46:45.131
JEFF: Shit.

46:46.602 --> 46:47.961
-(CAR THUDS)
-Oh, shit!

46:48.030 --> 46:49.396
You hit a car.

46:49.464 --> 46:51.870
I know I hit a car,
I can see that!

46:51.939 --> 46:53.366
I'm used
to my normal car's cameras

46:53.435 --> 46:55.673
and sensors and shit,
it beeps.

46:55.742 --> 46:57.011
I need the beeps!

46:58.873 --> 47:01.147
<i> (EVERYBODY'S HAPPY NOWADAYS</i>
BY BUZZCOCKS PLAYING)

47:04.817 --> 47:05.987
(DOORBELL RINGING)

47:07.383 --> 47:08.981
"Pizza was yummy.
Five stars!"

47:09.049 --> 47:10.585
Nice!

47:11.560 --> 47:13.194
They tipped you $1.15.

47:13.262 --> 47:14.655
Dicks!

47:16.395 --> 47:17.829
Jeff, Renee's getting antsy
about her poke bowl.

47:17.898 --> 47:19.526
Yeah, tell her
it's on the way.

47:19.594 --> 47:22.495
Why does she need
this poke bowl so soon?

47:22.564 --> 47:25.432
Let's pick up some
pad Thai for Martin.

47:25.501 --> 47:26.939
Can I use
your restroom real quick?

47:27.008 --> 47:28.441
MAN: Drivers can't
use the bathroom.

47:28.510 --> 47:30.613
Great, thanks.

47:30.682 --> 47:33.341
ROBOT: Order up!
I'm ready for my food.

47:33.410 --> 47:35.214
Oh, you got to be
fucking kidding me.

47:36.446 --> 47:38.316
You're serving this thing
before me?

47:39.955 --> 47:41.581
This is how the robots win,
you know.

47:41.650 --> 47:43.755
Jeff, Ashley's wondering
where the rigatoni is.

47:43.823 --> 47:44.891
Yeah, well, tell Ashley

47:44.960 --> 47:46.255
they gave her rigatoni
to the last guy

47:46.324 --> 47:47.693
and then they gave me
chicken parm,

47:47.761 --> 47:48.762
and now I got to go back

47:48.831 --> 47:49.896
to the place
to get her rigatoni

47:49.965 --> 47:51.725
while they make
a whole new rigatoni.

47:53.264 --> 47:54.702
Just tell her
it'll be there soon.

47:54.771 --> 47:55.799
-(HORN BEEPS)
-ROBOT: Look out!

47:55.868 --> 47:57.663
I'm coming through.

47:57.732 --> 47:59.040
<i> ♪ But I don't know</i>
<i> what it is ♪</i>

47:59.108 --> 48:03.439
<i> ♪ 'Cause everybody's</i>
<i> happy nowadays... ♪</i>

48:03.508 --> 48:05.780
Whoa, whoa, whoa.
Where's the extra ranch, homie?

48:05.848 --> 48:08.483
Oh, uh, I don't,
like, pack the bags.

48:08.552 --> 48:09.609
I just deliver them, so...

48:09.677 --> 48:10.984
Okay, but I can't
eat this amount of wings

48:11.052 --> 48:12.918
with this amount of ranch.
You understand?

48:12.987 --> 48:15.415
I agree that's not
enough ranch,

48:15.484 --> 48:16.549
but I don't know
what to tell you.

48:16.618 --> 48:19.219
Okay, well, one ranch,
one star, bitch.

48:19.287 --> 48:20.822
Please don't do that!

48:20.890 --> 48:21.898
Fuck!

48:23.228 --> 48:24.730
GABRIEL: We made
enough money, right?

48:24.798 --> 48:25.999
JEFF: Yeah, definitely.

48:26.068 --> 48:27.962
As long as this lady
lets us pay by phone,

48:28.031 --> 48:29.565
we're good.

48:32.242 --> 48:33.936
No.

48:34.005 --> 48:35.074
No, no, no, no, no!

48:35.142 --> 48:37.078
I don't get paid
till the end of the week?

48:38.378 --> 48:40.917
Don't these shitheads know
I need this money now?

48:43.347 --> 48:45.411
You know, with all
we spent on gas,

48:45.480 --> 48:47.220
we actually lost money today.

48:48.482 --> 48:50.058
Where are we going to sleep?

48:52.688 --> 48:56.321
Let's focus on the positives
about the car.

48:56.390 --> 48:57.425
It's tight on space,

48:57.493 --> 48:59.263
but since we've got
separate seats,

48:59.332 --> 49:01.696
it's like we each have
our own little beds.

49:03.604 --> 49:07.837
Maybe we could put
a little curtain up
in between for privacy.

49:07.906 --> 49:09.143
Could be cute.

49:10.247 --> 49:11.347
No.

49:11.416 --> 49:13.147
No curtain, okay.

49:14.676 --> 49:16.612
But will you promise
to think about it?

49:18.580 --> 49:19.989
Yeah, okay,
I'll think about it.

49:23.791 --> 49:26.956
You look stunning.

49:27.025 --> 49:28.061
You look ravishing.

49:28.129 --> 49:31.163
Listen, I have
a crazy question for you.

49:31.231 --> 49:33.466
Do you want to go
to Paris this weekend?

49:33.534 --> 49:34.832
What?

49:34.901 --> 49:36.538
Like "Paris" Paris?

49:36.607 --> 49:38.474
-This weekend?
-Yeah.

49:38.542 --> 49:40.632
I actually have, uh...

49:40.701 --> 49:42.240
(SIGHS) the union meeting.
I can't.

49:42.309 --> 49:44.505
But is there any way
we can go another time?

49:44.573 --> 49:47.881
Uh, it kinda has
to be this weekend.

49:47.950 --> 49:50.083
Why's it got to be
this weekend?

49:50.151 --> 49:53.348
I can't really explain,
but it just does.

49:53.417 --> 49:55.048
Could you blow off
the union thing?

49:55.117 --> 49:57.684
It took so long to get
everybody to believe
in this thing, I...

49:57.753 --> 49:59.694
I don't want them
to think I'm not serious.

49:59.762 --> 50:01.894
(ARJ GRUNTS IN FRUSTRATION)

50:01.963 --> 50:04.462
-What is that noise?
-It's...

50:05.326 --> 50:06.495
It's frustration

50:06.564 --> 50:08.067
'cause there's this
one version of our lives

50:08.136 --> 50:11.004
where we both go
to Paris this weekend,

50:11.072 --> 50:12.664
we have
this amazing time together.

50:12.733 --> 50:14.276
And instead,
you got to stay here

50:14.344 --> 50:17.412
and fight for better
working conditions
at Hardware Heaven.

50:17.481 --> 50:18.608
And that sucks.

50:19.275 --> 50:21.108
Why does it suck?

50:21.177 --> 50:22.612
It's my life.

50:22.680 --> 50:25.384
-I didn't mean it that way.
-No. I think you did.

50:27.281 --> 50:28.789
I get it.

50:28.858 --> 50:30.718
We live
two different lives.

50:30.787 --> 50:33.121
I live in my design studio
and sleep on a futon

50:33.190 --> 50:35.591
and you sleep here.

50:35.660 --> 50:39.199
But this is my life,
and I have to fight for it

50:39.268 --> 50:42.566
whether you think it's
worth fighting for or not.

50:43.497 --> 50:44.502
-Elena, I...
-No.

50:46.134 --> 50:47.142
Save it.

50:48.271 --> 50:49.342
I'm going to go home.

51:13.399 --> 51:14.502
-(COLLISION ALARM BEEPING)
-(HORN BLARING)

51:14.571 --> 51:16.028
(ARJ SCREAMING)

51:20.335 --> 51:22.302
Got some snacks!

51:22.371 --> 51:23.508
We have a problem.

51:24.307 --> 51:25.845
-What?
-It's Arj.

51:25.914 --> 51:27.846
I spoke with a colleague.

51:27.915 --> 51:29.184
He had an accident.

51:29.982 --> 51:31.453
He's in a coma.

51:31.522 --> 51:33.754
He's in a coma?

51:33.822 --> 51:35.691
What happened to him?

51:35.759 --> 51:37.621
He was texting and driving.

51:38.362 --> 51:39.456
What?

51:39.524 --> 51:41.091
I... I thought that was
your whole thing,

51:41.159 --> 51:42.831
to not let that happen!

51:42.900 --> 51:44.698
I'm here.
I couldn't save him.

51:44.767 --> 51:46.331
So what happens now?

51:46.400 --> 51:49.367
We have to wait
till he gets out of the coma.

51:49.435 --> 51:51.536
He has to be the one
who wants to switch.

51:53.275 --> 51:56.944
I agreed to switch lives
with him for a few days

51:57.013 --> 51:58.339
out of the kindness
of my heart

51:58.408 --> 51:59.780
so he could have some fun.

51:59.848 --> 52:02.115
This cannot be the deal!

52:02.183 --> 52:04.453
I cannot be like this
any longer!

52:04.522 --> 52:05.881
I don't like it!

52:05.949 --> 52:08.118
You go talk
to your angel friends,
and you fix this.

52:08.187 --> 52:09.884
You fix this for me, okay?

52:10.727 --> 52:12.623
-I will.
-Thank you!

52:13.529 --> 52:15.058
Gabriel.

52:15.127 --> 52:16.531
You've been let go.

52:16.600 --> 52:18.901
What? I'm fired?

52:18.970 --> 52:21.636
This is too big a mess
you've created.

52:21.705 --> 52:23.631
What happens to me?

52:23.699 --> 52:26.466
You live out this life
as a human.

52:26.535 --> 52:27.968
There must be another way.

52:29.044 --> 52:31.709
If Arj decides
to switch back

52:31.777 --> 52:36.917
and have hope for his life,
then you and Jeff are fine.

52:36.986 --> 52:39.980
But until then,
you're human.

52:41.417 --> 52:43.382
I already feel it.

52:43.451 --> 52:45.056
I'm perspiring.

52:45.124 --> 52:47.554
I... I need deodorant.

52:47.623 --> 52:49.860
And my stomach
feels strange.

52:49.929 --> 52:51.159
I think...

52:51.228 --> 52:52.630
I'm hungry?

52:57.173 --> 52:59.802
How will I know
when I'm done chewing?

53:01.442 --> 53:04.112
Oh, you've never eaten
anything before, huh?

53:04.180 --> 53:08.281
Um, you know,
I think you'll just know.

53:08.349 --> 53:10.918
What if I choke?
I've seen it happen a lot.

53:10.987 --> 53:13.618
Just eat
the hamburger, okay?

53:23.524 --> 53:24.959
-Wow.
-Yeah?

53:26.101 --> 53:28.234
-This is nice.
-(CHUCKLES)

53:28.303 --> 53:29.903
It's like nothing
I've experienced.

53:29.971 --> 53:32.070
(CHUCKLING) Yeah, man.

53:32.139 --> 53:34.639
No? Have a chicken nuggie.

53:42.679 --> 53:44.785
There you go!
It happened, see?

53:44.854 --> 53:46.447
Instinct kicked in.

53:46.516 --> 53:48.587
-Oh. (CHUCKLES)
-Yeah!

53:49.784 --> 53:52.388
-I like this even more.
-Yeah.

53:52.457 --> 53:54.153
-Have some milkshake.
-Mmm.

54:01.728 --> 54:04.639
-Wow.
-(CHUCKLES)

54:04.708 --> 54:08.777
Jeff, could you imagine
seeing strawberries
for thousands of years

54:08.845 --> 54:13.348
but never actually knowing
the sweet taste enclosed
in those magical berries?

54:14.047 --> 54:15.350
I can't imagine.

54:15.418 --> 54:17.517
And in all fairness,
that's a chocolate milkshake.

54:19.553 --> 54:22.318
What are we going to do, Jeff?
I'm scared.

54:22.386 --> 54:23.420
We don't have any money,

54:23.489 --> 54:25.822
and I'm already
perspiring a lot.

54:25.891 --> 54:29.294
So I looked up online
how long the average coma lasts.

54:29.363 --> 54:32.194
Two weeks.
Not that bad, you know.

54:32.263 --> 54:34.927
So we just got to make
enough money to last
until this guy wakes up.

54:34.996 --> 54:36.967
Tomorrow, I'll go
to my old office.

54:37.036 --> 54:39.634
I know everything
about all the companies
they've invested in.

54:39.703 --> 54:41.275
So, I'll give them
some insight

54:41.343 --> 54:43.373
that makes me look
like a financial genius.

54:43.441 --> 54:44.706
They'll hire me on the spot.

54:44.775 --> 54:46.510
It'll be enough money
for both of us.

54:46.578 --> 54:48.977
We'll be out
of that motel tomorrow.

54:52.789 --> 54:53.784
There you go.

54:54.351 --> 54:55.483
There you go!

54:55.551 --> 54:57.488
You're a big boy, huh?

54:57.556 --> 54:59.518
-Yeah, I'm a big boy.
-(CHUCKLES)

54:59.587 --> 55:00.791
You sure are.

55:02.296 --> 55:04.894
Let go of me!
Let go of me!

55:07.068 --> 55:08.960
Did you get the job?

55:09.029 --> 55:11.000
Does it look like
I got the job?

55:11.069 --> 55:12.240
No!

55:12.309 --> 55:14.033
They accused me
of hacking into their files,

55:14.102 --> 55:16.745
and then they basically
threatened to kill me.

55:16.813 --> 55:18.413
-Oh, no.
-Yeah.

55:19.409 --> 55:21.348
Chicken nuggie?

55:21.417 --> 55:25.985
Yes, of course I respect
patient confidentiality.

55:26.054 --> 55:27.522
I just need to know,

55:27.591 --> 55:31.225
do you have
any Indian dudes there
that are in a coma?

55:31.294 --> 55:33.552
Yes, I've actually
called many times.

55:33.621 --> 55:35.496
Hello? Hello?

55:37.663 --> 55:38.924
I don't think
they're going to tell me

55:38.993 --> 55:40.996
any more information
about this.

55:41.905 --> 55:43.105
It's been three weeks,

55:43.173 --> 55:45.534
I've applied
for one million jobs.

55:45.603 --> 55:47.099
I either
don't hear back at all

55:47.167 --> 55:48.440
or it's a scam
where people just want me

55:48.508 --> 55:50.771
to send them pictures
of my feet.

55:50.840 --> 55:52.645
Are you listening
to me, Gabriel?

55:53.910 --> 55:56.677
Sorry. The Internet
is amazing, Jeff.

55:56.746 --> 55:58.552
I want
to help you find jobs,

55:58.620 --> 56:01.447
but I also want to look
at photos of baby elephants.

56:01.516 --> 56:02.586
(CHUCKLES)

56:02.655 --> 56:05.189
Look at this guy,
bathing in a river.

56:05.258 --> 56:06.593
His name's Oliver.

56:06.661 --> 56:09.261
I cannot financially support
the both of us anymore.

56:09.330 --> 56:10.964
You have to get
a job, Gabriel.

56:11.032 --> 56:12.595
-A job?
-Yeah.

56:12.664 --> 56:15.728
Wow.
Wonder what I want to be.

56:15.797 --> 56:18.030
An architect, a scientist.

56:18.098 --> 56:19.507
Maybe I want
to work with animals.

56:20.105 --> 56:21.132
Oh.

56:21.201 --> 56:23.203
Maybe I could work
with baby elephants.

56:24.010 --> 56:25.007
Maybe.

56:26.279 --> 56:27.443
But probably not.

56:27.512 --> 56:28.545
FELIPE: Come on, Gabriel.

56:28.614 --> 56:30.243
You need to move
more fast, please.

56:31.845 --> 56:32.879
Do we do any other stuff

56:32.948 --> 56:34.419
or is it just dishes
all night?

56:34.488 --> 56:36.249
Just washing
dishes all night.

56:40.226 --> 56:42.128
My first check.

56:42.196 --> 56:44.458
Felipe, my first check.

56:44.527 --> 56:45.533
Good, Gabe.

56:47.366 --> 56:48.997
You're shitting me.

56:49.066 --> 56:51.966
Felipe, there's something
wrong with my check!

56:52.035 --> 56:54.474
FELIPE: What's wrong
with your check, Gabe?

56:54.543 --> 56:57.572
There's not enough money.
Where's the money?

56:57.641 --> 56:59.174
They're paying one number,

56:59.243 --> 57:02.279
and then taking a lot of money
for all these other things.

57:02.348 --> 57:03.584
Let me see, Gabe.

57:05.249 --> 57:08.257
This money goes
to the local government,
federal government,

57:08.325 --> 57:09.948
your insurance,
and your social security.

57:10.016 --> 57:11.053
That's why it's less money.

57:12.891 --> 57:15.121
I can't make enough money
to live off this.

57:15.189 --> 57:17.029
FELIPE: You may need
to get another job.

57:17.098 --> 57:18.500
Another job?

57:18.569 --> 57:21.633
I wash dishes all the time.
When can I do another job?

57:21.701 --> 57:23.472
FELIPE: I don't know.
I have three jobs.

57:26.406 --> 57:28.172
-What?
-I work here,

57:28.241 --> 57:29.839
I'm a mechanic,

57:29.907 --> 57:33.207
and I do valet parking
at an escape room.

57:33.276 --> 57:36.549
I thought a job gives me
enough money for all my things

57:36.618 --> 57:40.155
and some extra money
to spend on fun stuff.

57:40.224 --> 57:42.755
Sorry, Gabe.
This is how it is.

57:53.599 --> 57:55.897
-How you feeling?
-I'm good.

57:55.966 --> 57:59.131
It's a big day tomorrow.
Are you excited?

57:59.200 --> 58:03.141
-Yeah. Ready to go home.
-That's good.

58:03.210 --> 58:04.907
So, listen.

58:04.976 --> 58:06.842
Since you've been here,
there have been two guys

58:06.910 --> 58:08.808
who've been
asking around about you,

58:08.877 --> 58:10.646
seemed a little bit shady.

58:10.715 --> 58:13.582
One, curly hair,
pretty bland.

58:13.651 --> 58:15.516
The other guy, long hair,

58:15.585 --> 58:17.558
very attractive.

58:17.627 --> 58:19.689
He's kinda like a bad boy,
but with a soft touch.

58:19.758 --> 58:21.220
I know who you're
talking about.

58:21.288 --> 58:23.693
-Yes, I know them.
-Maybe give them a call.

58:23.762 --> 58:25.432
They seemed
pretty concerned.

58:25.501 --> 58:27.430
You could give
the tall one my number.

58:27.499 --> 58:28.768
That's fine with me.

58:31.239 --> 58:33.034
Can I ask you something?

58:33.102 --> 58:35.034
When people have
accidents like this, do...

58:35.103 --> 58:36.941
Do they ever have
memory issues?

58:41.479 --> 58:43.414
(ROBOT BEEPS)

58:43.483 --> 58:44.883
JEFF: Where is this place?

58:46.683 --> 58:48.924
"Stone Canyon Road"?

58:48.993 --> 58:50.559
That's my address.

58:51.853 --> 58:53.727
"Delivery for Arj"?

58:54.526 --> 58:56.460
He's out of the coma.

58:56.528 --> 58:58.160
He's out of the coma!

59:00.301 --> 59:03.904
(DOORBELL RINGING)

59:03.973 --> 59:05.205
ARJ: Jeff?

59:05.274 --> 59:06.875
The fuck is he doing here?

59:06.944 --> 59:07.906
(PHONE CHIMES)

59:08.969 --> 59:10.909
He's my Foodzr driver?

59:17.846 --> 59:19.049
Hey, thanks so much.

59:19.982 --> 59:21.248
What is
happening right now?

59:21.317 --> 59:23.620
You're out of the coma
and you're ordering ramen?

59:23.689 --> 59:25.151
Why didn't you
phone me, Arj?

59:25.220 --> 59:27.960
(SIGHS) They said
this might happen.

59:28.029 --> 59:30.630
Because of the coma,
I've been having
some memory issues.

59:30.698 --> 59:32.832
I'm so sorry,
but I don't remember you.

59:33.532 --> 59:35.503
You don't remember me?

59:35.571 --> 59:37.672
The pamphlet.
Let me get you a pamphlet.

59:44.080 --> 59:45.105
Here you go.

59:45.174 --> 59:47.478
It's called
dissociative memory loss.

59:47.547 --> 59:51.518
It's due to the medications
they were using to treat me
after the accident.

59:51.587 --> 59:54.145
It was pretty serious
brain trauma.

59:54.214 --> 59:55.289
Are you
fucking with me, man?

59:55.358 --> 59:56.621
Do you actually
not remember me?

59:56.690 --> 59:58.490
Maybe we can try
to jog my memory.

59:58.558 --> 01:00:00.261
-What's your name?
-Jeff!

01:00:00.330 --> 01:00:04.022
Uh, that's not
ringing a bell.

01:00:04.090 --> 01:00:05.425
You don't know who I am?

01:00:05.494 --> 01:00:07.931
If you read the pamphlet,
it could be very helpful.

01:00:08.000 --> 01:00:09.669
JEFF: "The duration
of memory loss can vary

01:00:09.738 --> 01:00:12.434
"depending on the specific
cause of the coma.

01:00:12.502 --> 01:00:15.606
"In some cases,
memory may improve
over time with treatment.

01:00:15.675 --> 01:00:17.569
"In other cases,
memory loss...

01:00:18.874 --> 01:00:20.209
"may be permanent."

01:00:20.884 --> 01:00:22.281
Wow.

01:00:22.349 --> 01:00:23.575
That's<i> no bueno.</i>

01:00:25.522 --> 01:00:27.656
Did you just say,
"That's<i> no bueno"?</i>

01:00:28.821 --> 01:00:31.383
No fucking shit,
it's<i> no bueno!</i>

01:00:31.451 --> 01:00:35.397
It's<i> muy, muy,</i>
<i> muy no bueno,</i> Gabriel.

01:00:35.466 --> 01:00:37.732
You know what?
I want to talk to God.

01:00:37.800 --> 01:00:39.894
Get me God.
I want a meeting
with God right now.

01:00:39.963 --> 01:00:41.229
That's above
my pay grade.

01:00:41.298 --> 01:00:42.728
Well, then who's your boss?
Who do you work for?

01:00:42.796 --> 01:00:44.136
Martha.

01:00:44.204 --> 01:00:45.539
Martha?

01:00:45.608 --> 01:00:47.876
You work for an angel
named Martha?

01:00:47.944 --> 01:00:49.139
Martha.

01:00:50.271 --> 01:00:51.641
What has happened
to you, Gabriel?

01:00:51.709 --> 01:00:52.907
You've just given up.

01:00:52.976 --> 01:00:54.309
You're smoking
cigarettes now?

01:00:54.377 --> 01:00:57.917
Leave me alone, Jeff.
I like it. It's all I have.

01:00:59.752 --> 01:01:01.216
Please don't
give up on me.

01:01:01.285 --> 01:01:03.887
Do you want to wash dishes
and smoke cigarettes

01:01:03.956 --> 01:01:05.420
or do you want
to get your wings back?

01:01:05.488 --> 01:01:08.620
You can get them back, man.
I know you can. Just think!

01:01:13.797 --> 01:01:15.671
His friend Elena.

01:01:15.739 --> 01:01:17.506
She was the one I was
supposed to help originally,

01:01:17.574 --> 01:01:20.509
but I didn't,
and she went off her path.

01:01:20.577 --> 01:01:23.545
Maybe I can help her
get back on her path

01:01:23.614 --> 01:01:26.206
and that'll help Arj
get back on his path.

01:01:26.274 --> 01:01:27.877
And then he'll want
to switch back.

01:01:27.946 --> 01:01:30.243
And then I'll get
my wings back.

01:01:30.311 --> 01:01:32.445
And then you'll get
your life back!

01:01:32.514 --> 01:01:34.786
That's what I want.
I knew you could do it, man!

01:01:34.855 --> 01:01:36.182
Good job. You can
do this, Gabriel.

01:01:36.251 --> 01:01:37.417
-Yes, yes.
-FELIPE: Hey, Gabriel,

01:01:37.486 --> 01:01:38.885
what are you doing there?
Your break is over.

01:01:38.954 --> 01:01:40.422
I need you, please.

01:01:40.491 --> 01:01:43.364
-You need to come back
to the restaurant.
-Okay, Felipe.

01:01:43.433 --> 01:01:44.898
I got to finish
my shift first.

01:01:47.368 --> 01:01:49.034
Thanks, man.

01:02:00.881 --> 01:02:04.385
That right there,
that's the truth.

01:02:04.454 --> 01:02:06.280
I had a union
at my last job,

01:02:06.349 --> 01:02:07.816
all they did was take money
out our checks,

01:02:07.884 --> 01:02:10.056
ain't do nothing for us.

01:02:10.125 --> 01:02:12.626
But, Kirby,
how could you say that
when that's not even us?

01:02:12.694 --> 01:02:14.890
Sounds like
the same nonsense to me.

01:02:14.959 --> 01:02:17.456
If that's not the truth,
what is?

01:02:17.525 --> 01:02:19.898
The truth is that one
of our team members

01:02:19.966 --> 01:02:22.604
had a panic attack
on the floor last week,

01:02:22.672 --> 01:02:24.130
picking and choosing
which bills to pay,

01:02:24.199 --> 01:02:25.798
worried about
getting evicted.

01:02:25.867 --> 01:02:27.534
And I know
she's not the only one
that has to deal with this.

01:02:28.545 --> 01:02:29.839
I mean, guys,
they're giving us

01:02:29.908 --> 01:02:31.975
more and more
double shifts,

01:02:32.044 --> 01:02:34.447
less training,
more responsibilities.

01:02:34.516 --> 01:02:35.783
And what do we get for it?

01:02:35.852 --> 01:02:38.583
Twenty-five cents a raise
and a pat on the back?

01:02:38.652 --> 01:02:42.315
It is very possible for this
place to take care of itself
and the people in it,

01:02:42.384 --> 01:02:43.755
but they keep giving us
less and less

01:02:43.824 --> 01:02:46.591
because we're okay
taking crumbs.

01:02:46.660 --> 01:02:48.287
So what's it going to be?

01:02:48.356 --> 01:02:50.530
Are we going
to take the crumbs?

01:02:50.599 --> 01:02:53.431
Or are we going
to fuck 'em up?

01:02:53.500 --> 01:02:54.803
(ALL APPLAUDING)

01:02:55.931 --> 01:02:56.937
GABRIEL: Yeah!

01:02:58.374 --> 01:03:00.601
And you know what else?

01:03:00.670 --> 01:03:04.703
Why do we need to give money
to taxes and social security?

01:03:05.912 --> 01:03:09.012
That money needs
to go to fun stuff,

01:03:09.080 --> 01:03:11.743
like chicken nuggies
and milkshakes.

01:03:13.086 --> 01:03:15.949
Milkshakes are good,
chicken nuggies are good.

01:03:16.018 --> 01:03:17.883
That's the truth.

01:03:17.952 --> 01:03:19.289
And dogs.

01:03:19.357 --> 01:03:21.453
I petted a dog
for the first time
the other day.

01:03:21.522 --> 01:03:24.127
Maybe they need
to get benefits, too.

01:03:24.196 --> 01:03:26.325
They give so much joy,
and what do they get?

01:03:26.394 --> 01:03:28.463
A pat on the head
and a biscuit.

01:03:29.437 --> 01:03:31.129
It's not enough!

01:03:31.198 --> 01:03:33.300
We can do better.

01:03:33.368 --> 01:03:36.334
And Hardware Heaven
can do better.

01:03:36.402 --> 01:03:40.174
For us
and for the dogs.

01:03:40.243 --> 01:03:42.648
ELENA: (CHUCKLES)
Hey, brother.

01:03:42.717 --> 01:03:44.683
What department
you work in?

01:03:44.752 --> 01:03:47.012
GABRIEL:
Oh, I don't work here.

01:03:47.081 --> 01:03:48.384
I'm a dishwasher

01:03:48.452 --> 01:03:50.089
at an all-you-can-eat
Korean barbecue restaurant.

01:03:51.661 --> 01:03:53.488
Am I not supposed
to be here?

01:04:05.572 --> 01:04:06.666
WOMAN: Yes.

01:04:08.111 --> 01:04:09.108
No.

01:04:10.839 --> 01:04:12.111
No.

01:04:13.149 --> 01:04:14.278
No.

01:04:15.250 --> 01:04:16.280
No.

01:04:17.351 --> 01:04:18.381
No.

01:04:19.012 --> 01:04:20.053
No.

01:04:43.710 --> 01:04:44.913
You're okay, Gabe?

01:04:46.679 --> 01:04:48.048
Hey, Felipe.

01:04:49.286 --> 01:04:51.348
No, I'm not.

01:04:53.389 --> 01:04:54.923
I'm just sad.

01:04:56.052 --> 01:04:58.254
I messed things up.

01:04:58.322 --> 01:05:00.955
That's why I got fired
from my last job.

01:05:01.024 --> 01:05:02.227
What did you did?

01:05:03.564 --> 01:05:05.659
I was an angel.

01:05:05.727 --> 01:05:09.633
I saved people when they were
texting and driving.

01:05:09.702 --> 01:05:11.940
Oh, cool, nice.

01:05:13.806 --> 01:05:15.138
Come on, Gabriel.

01:05:15.206 --> 01:05:17.273
Maybe you can
put your drink down.

01:05:17.341 --> 01:05:19.772
You can't be like this.
What do you want?

01:05:27.490 --> 01:05:29.683
I want my old job back.

01:05:31.860 --> 01:05:34.824
I want to fix
what I messed up.

01:05:34.893 --> 01:05:36.393
Then let's do it.

01:05:37.557 --> 01:05:40.758
You're a handsome,
sweet man.

01:05:40.827 --> 01:05:44.638
I believe in you,
but you're in a bad place.

01:05:44.707 --> 01:05:46.535
We need
to boost your spirits.

01:05:48.011 --> 01:05:50.869
What are you going to do
tonight after your shift?

01:05:52.515 --> 01:05:55.174
I don't know. Why?

01:05:55.243 --> 01:05:56.611
Let's go dancing.

01:05:56.680 --> 01:05:57.984
<i> (LA CANALLA</i> BY EL SUPER SHOW
DE LOS VAZKEZ PLAYING)

01:05:58.053 --> 01:05:59.812
GABRIEL: What do I do?
FELIPE: Just follow me.

01:06:04.020 --> 01:06:04.993
Have some tacos.

01:06:08.627 --> 01:06:09.921
Wow!

01:06:12.867 --> 01:06:14.334
You were
texting and driving.

01:06:14.402 --> 01:06:15.634
What?

01:06:15.703 --> 01:06:17.636
(TIRES SCREECHING)

01:06:17.705 --> 01:06:19.601
(SIGHS IN RELIEF)

01:06:21.100 --> 01:06:23.974
Hey, Gabriel, that's my wife.
Don't make me get a hose.

01:06:24.043 --> 01:06:26.139
Calm down.
That's my<i> viejo.</i>

01:06:26.208 --> 01:06:27.180
(SPEAKING SPANISH)

01:06:28.212 --> 01:06:29.579
(IN ENGLISH)
Thank you, Gabe.

01:06:29.648 --> 01:06:31.448
Bye.

01:06:32.818 --> 01:06:34.286
I saved her.

01:06:41.623 --> 01:06:43.460
This motherfucker
stole my vacation.

01:06:44.425 --> 01:06:45.927
I hope you're having fun.

01:06:45.996 --> 01:06:47.101
(PHONE CHIMES)

01:06:49.234 --> 01:06:51.271
"Dear valued
Foodzr associate,

01:06:51.339 --> 01:06:54.909
"next week, we are shifting
to primarily robo delivery.

01:06:54.978 --> 01:06:57.174
"Your rating does not
meet our threshold"?

01:06:57.243 --> 01:07:01.676
"Your account is
terminated immediately."

01:07:02.813 --> 01:07:04.384
Fuck!

01:07:04.452 --> 01:07:05.946
Fuck!

01:07:06.014 --> 01:07:07.413
Fuck!

01:07:07.482 --> 01:07:09.387
-GABRIEL: Jeff?
-JEFF: Yeah!

01:07:10.691 --> 01:07:11.785
What's wrong?

01:07:16.192 --> 01:07:19.029
This is too hard, man.

01:07:19.098 --> 01:07:20.625
Like, how do
people do this?

01:07:20.694 --> 01:07:23.934
How is everyone
not just miserable

01:07:24.002 --> 01:07:27.973
and angry all the time?

01:07:28.042 --> 01:07:29.273
I don't even
have it that bad,

01:07:29.342 --> 01:07:31.979
and I'm barely hanging on
by a thread here.

01:07:32.048 --> 01:07:36.249
In my old life,
all I did was go on vacation,

01:07:36.318 --> 01:07:41.085
and attend very, very easy
and pleasant Zoom meetings.

01:07:41.154 --> 01:07:43.388
-I want that back!
-(SIREN CHIRPS)

01:07:45.486 --> 01:07:47.485
JEFF: Shit, it's the pigs.

01:07:47.554 --> 01:07:50.293
Just what we fucking need!

01:07:50.362 --> 01:07:52.392
Explain to me
how I get my car back?

01:07:52.460 --> 01:07:53.494
Go down to the impound lot,

01:07:53.563 --> 01:07:55.261
pay all of your unpaid
parking tickets

01:07:55.330 --> 01:07:56.764
and the impound fee.

01:07:56.832 --> 01:08:00.102
Each day your car stays there,
impound fee goes up.

01:08:00.170 --> 01:08:02.242
Great system. Thank you.

01:08:05.210 --> 01:08:07.912
This same thing
happened to Arj.

01:08:07.980 --> 01:08:09.808
What? What do you mean?

01:08:09.877 --> 01:08:12.150
After you fired him,
he went to donate plasma

01:08:12.219 --> 01:08:13.646
and then he passed out
at a Denny's,

01:08:13.715 --> 01:08:16.014
and when he woke up,
his car was towed.

01:08:17.857 --> 01:08:18.852
JEFF: Weird.

01:08:21.224 --> 01:08:22.526
What are we going to do?

01:08:24.195 --> 01:08:26.528
I really don't know, man.

01:08:26.596 --> 01:08:30.035
We have nowhere to live.
I have no job now.

01:08:30.104 --> 01:08:32.305
We just really need
some money.

01:08:43.247 --> 01:08:45.717
-What?
-Pretty Baby.

01:08:45.786 --> 01:08:46.852
My watches.

01:08:46.920 --> 01:08:48.854
We can get my watches!

01:08:48.923 --> 01:08:50.314
-Your watches?
-Yeah!

01:08:50.383 --> 01:08:51.620
Let's go!

01:08:51.689 --> 01:08:54.190
<i> (GROOVE IS IN THE HEART</i>
BY DEEE-LITE PLAYING)

01:08:54.259 --> 01:08:55.922
GABRIEL:
What's going on here?

01:08:56.556 --> 01:08:57.924
It's my birthday.

01:08:58.733 --> 01:08:59.797
GABRIEL: Oh.

01:08:59.866 --> 01:09:00.867
Happy birthday.

01:09:00.936 --> 01:09:02.462
No, it's Arj's
birthday now,

01:09:02.531 --> 01:09:04.839
he stole
my 40th birthday party!

01:09:04.908 --> 01:09:05.965
I don't even know
my birthday.

01:09:07.870 --> 01:09:10.241
Are we still going to be able
to get the watches?

01:09:10.309 --> 01:09:12.044
Yeah, he doesn't
remember who we are.

01:09:12.113 --> 01:09:13.812
It's fine.
This is actually good.

01:09:13.881 --> 01:09:14.872
I sneak upstairs.

01:09:14.941 --> 01:09:16.414
I still remember the code
to the safe.

01:09:16.483 --> 01:09:18.912
If I can get Pretty Baby,
we're set for life.

01:09:20.222 --> 01:09:23.717
I still feel bad about
(SOFTLY) the stealing.

01:09:23.786 --> 01:09:28.154
It's not stealing
because all this is mine!

01:09:28.222 --> 01:09:29.296
Come on!

01:09:30.490 --> 01:09:31.628
That's true.

01:09:33.769 --> 01:09:34.759
(PEOPLE CHEERING)

01:09:34.828 --> 01:09:36.431
Oh, you got
to be kidding me.

01:09:36.500 --> 01:09:38.870
<i> ♪ Groove is in the heart ♪</i>

01:09:38.939 --> 01:09:40.765
He stole my routine!

01:09:40.834 --> 01:09:42.205
<i> ♪ Groove is in the heart ♪</i>

01:09:42.274 --> 01:09:44.307
This whole thing
was my idea!

01:09:44.376 --> 01:09:47.014
<i> ♪ Groove is in the heart ♪</i>

01:09:47.083 --> 01:09:49.716
You did this.
You ruined my birthday.

01:09:49.785 --> 01:09:52.345
Jeff, the watches.

01:09:52.414 --> 01:09:53.452
Yeah, okay, okay.

01:09:55.014 --> 01:09:56.750
There's some guys
guarding the stairs.

01:09:56.819 --> 01:09:58.617
I'm going to do a lap,
try to wait them out,

01:09:58.685 --> 01:10:00.387
maybe hit that buffet table.

01:10:00.456 --> 01:10:01.727
He even stole my caterer!

01:10:01.796 --> 01:10:03.257
Goddamn it.

01:10:03.326 --> 01:10:04.526
Yeah, I'll be back.

01:10:04.595 --> 01:10:06.234
You, you know,
do your thing. Blend in.

01:10:08.070 --> 01:10:11.468
<i>♪ I couldn't ask for another ♪</i>

01:10:11.537 --> 01:10:14.506
<i> ♪ No, I couldn't</i>
<i> ask for another ♪</i>

01:10:15.605 --> 01:10:17.871
<i> ♪ DJ Soul was on a roll ♪</i>

01:10:17.940 --> 01:10:19.770
<i> ♪ I've been told</i>
<i> he can't be sold ♪</i>

01:10:19.839 --> 01:10:20.882
<i> ♪ He's not vicious... ♪</i>

01:10:20.951 --> 01:10:22.641
She smelled
like blueberries.

01:10:22.710 --> 01:10:24.048
ARJ: I'll see you later,
Leonard.

01:10:24.116 --> 01:10:27.149
His friend from the gym?

01:10:27.218 --> 01:10:28.817
Hello! How are you?

01:10:30.318 --> 01:10:32.119
I'm good.

01:10:32.187 --> 01:10:35.289
ARJ: (OVER MIC)<i> It's not my</i>
<i> birthday, it's your birthday!</i>

01:10:35.358 --> 01:10:36.825
(PEOPLE CHEERING)

01:10:37.567 --> 01:10:39.595
Arj's dad?

01:10:39.664 --> 01:10:42.429
<i> Come on, let's go!</i>
<i> Let's go! Let's go!</i>

01:10:42.497 --> 01:10:44.404
<i> Let's go! Let's go!</i>

01:10:46.003 --> 01:10:47.165
Jeff?

01:10:49.475 --> 01:10:51.142
No, Tanner,
what the fuck are you doing?

01:10:51.210 --> 01:10:53.313
Don't lean on the art, man!

01:10:53.382 --> 01:10:56.116
This is someone's painting,
for Christ's sakes.

01:10:56.185 --> 01:10:57.675
Why was I friends
with these assholes?

01:10:57.743 --> 01:10:59.577
Yo, Linda, what's up?

01:10:59.646 --> 01:11:01.786
Hey, do I know you?

01:11:01.854 --> 01:11:03.181
Oh, um,

01:11:03.249 --> 01:11:05.253
let's just say we knew
each other in another life.

01:11:05.321 --> 01:11:06.622
-Sick.
-Yeah.

01:11:06.691 --> 01:11:09.688
Do you know that guy,
he's got the long hair,

01:11:09.757 --> 01:11:10.788
-kinda tall.
-Yes. Uh-huh.

01:11:10.857 --> 01:11:12.163
Yeah, Gabriel.
He's an angel.

01:11:12.231 --> 01:11:13.791
-He's fucking hot.
-Yeah.

01:11:13.860 --> 01:11:15.629
I'm going to go
sit on his face.

01:11:15.698 --> 01:11:18.037
That will
really confuse him.

01:11:18.106 --> 01:11:20.033
-(MAN LAUGHING)
-Is Jeff here?

01:11:20.433 --> 01:11:22.037
Oh, no.

01:11:22.105 --> 01:11:23.537
But we got some
mushroom chocolates, dude.
You want a nibble?

01:11:23.605 --> 01:11:26.105
-Ooh, chocolate.
-Let's go.

01:11:27.913 --> 01:11:28.943
Thanks.

01:11:29.719 --> 01:11:31.512
Tastes funky.

01:11:31.581 --> 01:11:33.115
-Can I have another one?
-Sure.

01:11:33.184 --> 01:11:34.655
Go off, king.

01:11:34.724 --> 01:11:36.951
GABRIEL: Mmm.

01:11:37.019 --> 01:11:38.986
<i> (MADAME HOLLYWOOD</i>
BY FELIX DA HOUSECAT PLAYING)

01:11:42.292 --> 01:11:43.798
ARJ: Elena?

01:11:43.866 --> 01:11:45.155
What are you doing here?

01:11:45.224 --> 01:11:48.526
I am currently serving
some salmon crostini.

01:11:48.595 --> 01:11:49.698
Happy birthday.

01:11:49.766 --> 01:11:51.996
-Thanks. But what's...
-I started working

01:11:52.065 --> 01:11:53.639
for this catering company
on the side.

01:11:53.708 --> 01:11:56.003
I didn't know it was
your address till I got
to the house.

01:11:57.146 --> 01:11:58.876
-Oh.
-I got to get back to work.

01:11:58.945 --> 01:12:00.740
ARJ: W...

01:12:00.809 --> 01:12:02.581
Nice dance moves,
by the way.

01:12:07.890 --> 01:12:09.654
So, how do you know Arj?

01:12:11.257 --> 01:12:13.361
-Wow.
-(BOTH CHUCKLE)

01:12:14.328 --> 01:12:16.793
-I don't know if I can say.
-Oh.

01:12:17.592 --> 01:12:18.656
Can you keep a secret?

01:12:18.725 --> 01:12:20.662
Oh, I love secrets.

01:12:20.731 --> 01:12:23.761
(SOFTLY) Well, I used
to be an angel.

01:12:23.830 --> 01:12:25.664
And I switched Arj's life

01:12:25.733 --> 01:12:27.438
-with Jeff's life.
-Oh.

01:12:27.506 --> 01:12:30.003
But then Arj didn't
want to go back,

01:12:30.072 --> 01:12:33.604
and that's how I lost my wings
and became human.

01:12:33.673 --> 01:12:35.280
Oh, my God.

01:12:35.349 --> 01:12:37.114
Are we role-playing
right now?

01:12:37.183 --> 01:12:38.917
I want you so bad.

01:12:38.986 --> 01:12:40.118
-No.
-Huh?

01:12:40.187 --> 01:12:42.047
Oh. I got to go find Jeff.

01:12:42.115 --> 01:12:44.254
No, no, no, no, no, no.
Forget about Jeff.

01:12:44.322 --> 01:12:46.218
Tell me more secrets.

01:12:51.167 --> 01:12:53.926
Yo. What you doing here?
You okay?

01:12:53.995 --> 01:12:57.204
(SIGHS) I shouldn't
be here, Leonard.

01:12:57.273 --> 01:13:00.900
This house, this party,
it's not mine.

01:13:00.969 --> 01:13:02.572
It's like I stole it
from someone else.

01:13:02.641 --> 01:13:05.376
-The Native Americans?
-No, not them.

01:13:05.445 --> 01:13:07.641
Yo, anybody got
a setup like this,

01:13:07.709 --> 01:13:09.307
they stole it from somebody.

01:13:11.344 --> 01:13:13.217
Hey, did you see that server
that had long hair?

01:13:13.286 --> 01:13:14.653
-The Black girl?
-Yeah.

01:13:14.722 --> 01:13:16.249
What, 'cause I'm Black,
you think I know where she is?

01:13:16.318 --> 01:13:17.716
You think I can track
all the Black people
at your party?

01:13:17.784 --> 01:13:19.256
That's not what I meant.

01:13:19.324 --> 01:13:21.228
We went out a while ago.

01:13:21.296 --> 01:13:25.158
She's great.
But I'm just too fancy.

01:13:26.332 --> 01:13:27.864
It kinda pulled us apart.

01:13:28.398 --> 01:13:29.899
You are fancy.

01:13:30.797 --> 01:13:32.440
But you got heart.

01:13:32.508 --> 01:13:35.471
When you saw me, I was just
some dude on the street.

01:13:35.539 --> 01:13:37.672
And you got me an apartment.

01:13:37.741 --> 01:13:39.642
You got me
a custom-made tuxedo.

01:13:39.710 --> 01:13:41.145
I'm over here eating
salmon cros...

01:13:41.214 --> 01:13:42.481
cros... crossa...

01:13:42.550 --> 01:13:45.243
I can't even pronounce
the things I'm eating.

01:13:45.312 --> 01:13:47.950
Maybe she just don't know
who you really are.

01:13:52.692 --> 01:13:54.693
<i> (QUAND LA VILLE DORT</i>
BY NIAGARA PLAYING)

01:13:58.668 --> 01:13:59.731
Hey.

01:14:01.561 --> 01:14:02.635
Hey!

01:14:04.239 --> 01:14:05.829
Your party kinda winded down.

01:14:05.898 --> 01:14:07.106
(ARJ GROANS SOFTLY)

01:14:07.174 --> 01:14:09.235
Yeah, I guess it did.

01:14:10.177 --> 01:14:13.714
-You okay?
-Yeah.

01:14:13.782 --> 01:14:15.608
What are you doing now?
Do you want to hang out
for a minute?

01:14:15.677 --> 01:14:18.211
I got to clean up.

01:14:19.454 --> 01:14:21.456
It looks like
they're pretty much done.

01:14:22.753 --> 01:14:25.058
Come on, what,
do you hate me now?

01:14:25.126 --> 01:14:26.725
No, I don't hate you.

01:14:29.364 --> 01:14:30.459
You know, you're
the only person here

01:14:30.528 --> 01:14:31.528
I wanted to hang out with,

01:14:31.597 --> 01:14:35.165
and everyone else
is finally gone.

01:14:35.234 --> 01:14:36.295
What do you say?

01:14:38.600 --> 01:14:40.202
(ARJ STRAINS)

01:14:40.270 --> 01:14:41.904
(SIGHS)

01:14:41.973 --> 01:14:44.105
You want to dance?
We still got the disco floor.

01:15:00.019 --> 01:15:01.726
ELENA:<i> You were right.</i>

01:15:01.795 --> 01:15:04.221
<i> We should've gone to Paris.</i>
(CHUCKLES SOFTLY)

01:15:04.290 --> 01:15:06.267
<i> I thought I could</i>
<i> make a difference,</i>

01:15:06.336 --> 01:15:09.130
<i> but, uh,</i>
<i> it was a waste of time.</i>

01:15:10.534 --> 01:15:12.166
ARJ:<i> That's not true.</i>

01:15:13.435 --> 01:15:14.465
I lost.

01:15:16.476 --> 01:15:18.942
So what's your answer?
Give up?

01:15:21.273 --> 01:15:23.284
You're in a huge house
with a pool

01:15:23.353 --> 01:15:26.785
telling me not to give up,
to fight.

01:15:28.148 --> 01:15:30.224
How can I fight
a giant corporation

01:15:30.293 --> 01:15:32.318
when I'm fighting
just to get by?

01:15:33.996 --> 01:15:35.788
My rent went up.

01:15:35.857 --> 01:15:37.389
I lost my apartment. I...

01:15:38.763 --> 01:15:41.629
I'm sleeping
in my cousin's car, Arj.

01:15:41.697 --> 01:15:43.197
(ARJ EXHALES HEAVILY)

01:15:46.540 --> 01:15:48.307
You'll never
believe me, but...

01:15:48.376 --> 01:15:51.036
-(SIGHS)
-...I've been there.

01:15:51.105 --> 01:15:56.082
Even if you have,
you're here now.

01:15:56.151 --> 01:15:57.585
And it's beautiful.

01:15:59.352 --> 01:16:01.749
Damn! I want to go.

01:16:01.818 --> 01:16:03.756
I want to go
to Paris, but...

01:16:05.355 --> 01:16:06.352
(SIGHS)

01:16:08.125 --> 01:16:11.357
I know what's going on
on the ground down there.

01:16:14.193 --> 01:16:16.128
And instead
of being up here

01:16:16.197 --> 01:16:17.898
drinking the fanciest
wine you got,

01:16:17.967 --> 01:16:20.069
I guess I'd rather
be down there...

01:16:22.169 --> 01:16:24.271
fighting to get
more people up here,

01:16:25.378 --> 01:16:27.010
rather than just myself.

01:16:33.221 --> 01:16:34.622
(SIGHING) I got to go.

01:17:48.889 --> 01:17:50.258
Pretty Baby.

01:17:53.432 --> 01:17:55.263
(ZIPPING UP BAG)

01:17:59.108 --> 01:18:02.000
(ARJ SCREAMING)

01:18:02.068 --> 01:18:04.205
(GROANS) You shot me!

01:18:04.274 --> 01:18:07.546
-(JEFF SCREAMING)
-Oh, no, Jeff! Are you okay?

01:18:07.615 --> 01:18:09.047
(SCREAMING)
Why'd you shoot me?

01:18:09.115 --> 01:18:11.112
You said, "Don't hesitate.
Shoot first, questions later."

01:18:11.180 --> 01:18:13.721
I thought you were
a home invader on meth!

01:18:14.684 --> 01:18:15.822
I said that?

01:18:16.620 --> 01:18:18.189
You remember me?

01:18:18.257 --> 01:18:21.055
When I brought you
that ramen and gyoza,
you remembered me!

01:18:21.123 --> 01:18:22.691
-I knew it!
-(SCREAMS) I'm so sorry!

01:18:22.759 --> 01:18:23.894
I'm going to call 911!

01:18:23.963 --> 01:18:25.192
-I'm doing that now!
-You fucking asshole.

01:18:25.260 --> 01:18:27.729
I knew it! You lied to me
and you shot me!

01:18:27.797 --> 01:18:29.097
You're a bad man, Arj!

01:18:29.166 --> 01:18:31.764
(GRUNTS IN FRUSTRATION)
I can't find my phone!

01:18:31.833 --> 01:18:32.929
JEFF: Use mine!

01:18:32.998 --> 01:18:35.374
(SCREAMS)

01:18:35.443 --> 01:18:36.704
-Arj?
-(JEFF SCREAMS)

01:18:36.773 --> 01:18:37.975
Jeff, are you okay?

01:18:38.044 --> 01:18:40.270
Gabriel, call an angel
that deals with gunshots!

01:18:40.339 --> 01:18:41.639
I have no way
to contact them,

01:18:41.707 --> 01:18:43.583
and they usually work
in a different part of town.

01:18:43.651 --> 01:18:44.910
JEFF: I brought you
into my life,

01:18:44.979 --> 01:18:47.213
I gave you burrata,

01:18:47.282 --> 01:18:49.416
and then you took
everything from me.

01:18:51.859 --> 01:18:56.791
You lied to me,
you stole all my dance moves,

01:18:56.859 --> 01:18:58.194
and then you shot me.

01:19:00.365 --> 01:19:02.903
I'm sorry, man.
Why'd you have a gun
in the first place?

01:19:02.972 --> 01:19:05.297
Well, I didn't think I'd be
the one who'd get shot by it.

01:19:05.365 --> 01:19:06.902
Statistically,
you'd be surprised.

01:19:06.971 --> 01:19:09.876
Okay, not now.
Is that all right?

01:19:10.907 --> 01:19:12.406
Why did you lie to me, Arj?

01:19:14.216 --> 01:19:16.141
My life is hard.

01:19:16.210 --> 01:19:18.779
Yours is
really easy and fun.

01:19:18.848 --> 01:19:19.886
I couldn't go back.

01:19:20.984 --> 01:19:24.754
But it's gone on
long enough.

01:19:24.823 --> 01:19:27.685
Gabriel,
how do I switch back?

01:19:28.891 --> 01:19:30.259
Well, you've told me.

01:19:31.390 --> 01:19:32.456
If you want
to switch back

01:19:32.525 --> 01:19:33.724
to your old life,
it should happen.

01:19:34.602 --> 01:19:36.134
Well, why isn't it happening?

01:19:36.203 --> 01:19:39.666
You want to go back
because you feel guilty
about Jeff,

01:19:39.735 --> 01:19:44.240
but you still don't feel
your life, your real life,
is worth living.

01:19:44.940 --> 01:19:47.211
You don't have hope.

01:19:47.280 --> 01:19:50.214
Just to be clear, he does not
only have to want to go back,

01:19:50.283 --> 01:19:52.882
which was what I thought
we've been going for
this whole time,

01:19:52.951 --> 01:19:54.383
he has to be
psyched about it?

01:19:54.452 --> 01:19:55.786
Yes.

01:19:55.855 --> 01:19:57.451
Well, why would
that ever happen?

01:19:58.194 --> 01:20:00.021
No offense.

01:20:00.090 --> 01:20:02.321
I don't know
what else we can do.

01:20:02.390 --> 01:20:04.893
This has been
a very stressful week.

01:20:04.962 --> 01:20:06.592
Maybe we go back
to my house?

01:20:07.435 --> 01:20:08.660
Technically, your house.

01:20:09.765 --> 01:20:11.267
Our house?

01:20:12.404 --> 01:20:13.566
For now.

01:20:14.573 --> 01:20:15.635
Can I come?

01:20:15.704 --> 01:20:16.910
Yes.

01:20:19.774 --> 01:20:20.848
Like it?

01:20:21.941 --> 01:20:22.949
Yeah.

01:20:23.879 --> 01:20:25.711
I needed this.

01:20:25.779 --> 01:20:29.419
It's the back and forth that
really makes the experience.

01:20:29.487 --> 01:20:30.685
Yeah.

01:20:30.754 --> 01:20:33.050
Shall we plunge?

01:20:33.119 --> 01:20:34.723
What's that?

01:20:34.792 --> 01:20:36.329
Let's go! Let's go!

01:20:36.398 --> 01:20:38.325
(GABRIEL SCREAMS)

01:20:38.393 --> 01:20:39.657
-(TIMER BEEPING)
-You did it, two minutes!

01:20:39.726 --> 01:20:41.831
-You did it, you did it!
-Yeah, Gabriel! Let's go!

01:20:41.900 --> 01:20:43.770
-I'm getting in, too.
-Yep.

01:20:43.839 --> 01:20:45.098
<i> (BOYS (SUMMER TIME LOVE)</i>
BY SABRINA PLAYING)

01:20:45.166 --> 01:20:47.675
Oh, fuck,
I've been shot!

01:20:47.743 --> 01:20:49.635
I shouldn't do this.
I shouldn't do this.

01:20:49.704 --> 01:20:51.536
<i> ♪ Boys, boys, boys</i>
<i> Get ready for my love ♪</i>

01:20:51.605 --> 01:20:55.274
-(MIMICS DINOSAUR ROARING)
-(JEFF EXCLAIMING)

01:20:55.343 --> 01:20:57.243
<i> ♪ ...in summertime love ♪</i>

01:20:57.312 --> 01:21:00.448
<i> ♪ Be my lover, be my baby ♪</i>

01:21:02.089 --> 01:21:04.187
JEFF: You actually learned
to drive the Porsche?

01:21:04.256 --> 01:21:05.618
ARJ: Yeah. I mean,
I know how to drive manual.

01:21:05.686 --> 01:21:06.891
You got to...
You got to learn.
I'll teach you.

01:21:06.960 --> 01:21:09.292
JEFF: I do. Please do.
It looks so fun.

01:21:10.498 --> 01:21:11.899
Have a nice swim?

01:21:13.201 --> 01:21:14.960
Martha.

01:21:15.029 --> 01:21:17.128
Yeah, I guess.

01:21:17.197 --> 01:21:19.038
(MARTHA CHUCKLES)

01:21:19.106 --> 01:21:23.736
So, now Arj wants to go back,
but he still can't.

01:21:23.805 --> 01:21:25.711
Wow.

01:21:25.780 --> 01:21:29.112
I gave you
the easiest assignment.

01:21:29.181 --> 01:21:31.150
All you had to do was
give someone a nudge,

01:21:31.219 --> 01:21:34.253
they look right at the road,
and you were done for the day.

01:21:34.321 --> 01:21:35.654
I know.

01:21:35.723 --> 01:21:37.415
I just thought
I could do more.

01:21:37.484 --> 01:21:39.652
Oh, you certainly
have done more.

01:21:39.720 --> 01:21:42.926
You've been washing dishes,
eating chicken nuggies,

01:21:42.995 --> 01:21:46.323
smoking, drinking,
making speeches.

01:21:46.391 --> 01:21:48.593
Oh, I've seen it all.

01:21:48.661 --> 01:21:51.602
How do I get him to have
hope for his life?

01:21:51.671 --> 01:21:53.172
I lived like he did,

01:21:53.241 --> 01:21:56.242
I understand now why he didn't
have hope in the first place.

01:21:56.311 --> 01:21:57.868
Gabriel...

01:21:59.211 --> 01:22:02.582
sometimes a lost soul
doesn't need an angel.

01:22:02.651 --> 01:22:04.446
It just needs
another person.

01:22:06.213 --> 01:22:08.021
I don't understand.

01:22:09.048 --> 01:22:10.089
I know.

01:22:11.360 --> 01:22:12.388
But I have hope.

01:22:13.561 --> 01:22:14.753
ARJ: Hey, Gabriel!

01:22:16.431 --> 01:22:17.664
You hungry?

01:22:17.733 --> 01:22:20.033
-GABRIEL: Always.
-Let's eat.

01:22:32.046 --> 01:22:34.305
My two favorite things
since I've been a human

01:22:34.373 --> 01:22:37.681
are dancing and tacos.

01:22:37.750 --> 01:22:41.479
-I've been a human way longer,
still two of my favorites.
-JEFF: Mine too.

01:22:41.548 --> 01:22:44.090
-(WOMAN CHUCKLES)
-ARJ: Elena?

01:22:45.361 --> 01:22:47.189
Hey. One second.

01:22:47.257 --> 01:22:49.360
-How's it going?
-ARJ: Uh, I'm good.

01:22:49.428 --> 01:22:52.459
I'm just grabbing some tacos
with some pals. How are you?

01:22:52.527 --> 01:22:54.562
Good. Here with
the Hardware Heaven crew.

01:22:54.630 --> 01:22:56.566
We just had a meeting
and grabbing a bite to eat.

01:22:56.635 --> 01:22:58.171
A meeting?

01:22:58.240 --> 01:23:00.174
We're going
to give it another go
at organizing the store.

01:23:00.242 --> 01:23:01.802
You are?

01:23:01.870 --> 01:23:03.208
Yeah.

01:23:03.277 --> 01:23:05.908
I know I was down about it,
you know, last we talked.

01:23:05.976 --> 01:23:07.078
But I don't know, man,

01:23:07.146 --> 01:23:09.508
I just realized
that change is difficult.

01:23:09.577 --> 01:23:11.651
You're changing something,
you know.

01:23:11.720 --> 01:23:13.212
And no, we won't
win right away,

01:23:13.280 --> 01:23:14.886
but you keep fighting

01:23:14.955 --> 01:23:16.782
and fighting
and fighting, and...

01:23:18.123 --> 01:23:20.417
Because of that,
you eventually do.

01:23:20.485 --> 01:23:21.853
That's what I believe.

01:23:24.757 --> 01:23:26.525
We're going to grab
a drink after this.

01:23:26.593 --> 01:23:28.567
Do you know
any good spots nearby?

01:23:28.636 --> 01:23:29.795
GABRIEL: I know one.

01:23:31.837 --> 01:23:33.304
(CUMBIA MUSIC PLAYING)

01:23:42.341 --> 01:23:43.574
ELENA: Hey!

01:23:43.643 --> 01:23:44.717
I remember
where I know you from.

01:23:44.786 --> 01:23:46.017
You broke into
the break room.

01:23:46.086 --> 01:23:47.612
Uh, milkshake
and chicken nuggies guy.

01:23:47.681 --> 01:23:49.554
-That's you, right?
-Yeah, that's me.

01:23:49.623 --> 01:23:50.618
How's it going?

01:23:51.183 --> 01:23:52.191
Good.

01:23:56.588 --> 01:23:58.691
Whoa. Look at Gabriel go.

01:23:58.760 --> 01:24:02.066
He's got some moves.
He really got into cumbia.

01:24:02.134 --> 01:24:04.467
Everyone learned
to dance except me.

01:24:26.055 --> 01:24:27.061
ARJ: Gabriel.

01:24:28.530 --> 01:24:29.921
What's wrong?

01:24:33.359 --> 01:24:35.100
I'm a failure.

01:24:35.169 --> 01:24:38.901
I've put you and Jeff
in a terrible situation.

01:24:38.970 --> 01:24:40.603
It's all my fault.

01:24:40.671 --> 01:24:44.073
What? None of that's true.
You were just trying to help.

01:24:44.142 --> 01:24:46.338
My boss told me
I wasn't ready,

01:24:46.406 --> 01:24:48.038
and she knew the truth.

01:24:49.144 --> 01:24:50.216
What truth?

01:24:52.182 --> 01:24:53.787
That I'm kind of a dum-dum.

01:24:53.856 --> 01:24:55.920
A dum-dum?
You're not a dum-dum.

01:24:55.989 --> 01:24:57.986
I'm a dum-dum,
and I give up.

01:24:58.055 --> 01:24:59.317
You can't give up.

01:24:59.386 --> 01:25:02.095
-You did.
-(SIGHS)

01:25:02.164 --> 01:25:05.828
But, Gabriel, I lost my job,
I lost my apartment.

01:25:05.897 --> 01:25:07.196
I lost my job.

01:25:07.265 --> 01:25:09.428
I used to be
a celestial being,

01:25:09.496 --> 01:25:11.836
and now I'm a chain-smoker.

01:25:11.905 --> 01:25:14.301
I'm addicted to nicotine.

01:25:14.370 --> 01:25:16.975
Yeah, but it's not over,
is it?

01:25:17.044 --> 01:25:18.811
I mean, you came down
to show me

01:25:18.880 --> 01:25:20.712
that my life's
worth living.

01:25:20.781 --> 01:25:22.108
Come on, let's go.

01:25:22.177 --> 01:25:24.114
I tried, Arj.

01:25:24.183 --> 01:25:25.544
But it seems
you prefer to live

01:25:25.613 --> 01:25:27.647
in a giant mansion
with a pool

01:25:27.716 --> 01:25:31.486
to sleeping in your car
and eating protein bars.

01:25:31.555 --> 01:25:33.720
But, Gabriel, I never
wanted all that stuff.

01:25:33.789 --> 01:25:36.392
I just wanted enough,
enough to be comfortable,

01:25:36.461 --> 01:25:39.793
to not feel like I was
struggling all the time.

01:25:39.862 --> 01:25:44.198
If I go back,
will I have my car,
a job, anything?

01:25:44.266 --> 01:25:47.465
No to all those things.

01:25:47.534 --> 01:25:49.275
Well, that's pretty scary.

01:25:52.575 --> 01:25:55.477
When I got fired,
I was scared, too.

01:25:55.545 --> 01:25:58.182
I didn't know
what was going to happen.

01:25:58.250 --> 01:25:59.780
And a lot of times,
it wasn't fun.

01:26:01.649 --> 01:26:03.981
Sleeping in your car
wasn't fun,

01:26:04.050 --> 01:26:08.591
being hungry wasn't fun,
washing dishes wasn't fun.

01:26:09.123 --> 01:26:10.120
But...

01:26:11.898 --> 01:26:14.730
I love being human.

01:26:14.799 --> 01:26:19.264
I love dancing, I love tacos,
I love Felipe, I love Jeff.

01:26:19.333 --> 01:26:20.999
And I love you.

01:26:24.144 --> 01:26:26.042
If I go back,
what happens to you?

01:26:26.111 --> 01:26:27.677
Will I ever see you again?

01:26:27.746 --> 01:26:29.181
No.

01:26:29.250 --> 01:26:32.043
My job would be done,
I'll be an angel again.

01:26:33.314 --> 01:26:36.221
No more tacos.

01:26:36.290 --> 01:26:38.489
Maybe I'll leave one out
for you, just in case.

01:26:41.960 --> 01:26:43.054
(ARJ CHUCKLES)

01:26:44.158 --> 01:26:45.923
What?

01:26:45.991 --> 01:26:48.794
(SIGHS) One time,
I took my dad for tacos,

01:26:48.862 --> 01:26:50.532
and I got him this shirt
for his birthday,

01:26:50.601 --> 01:26:52.470
and he just spilled
green sauce all over it.

01:26:52.539 --> 01:26:55.865
Just completely ruined
the shirt, like a little kid.

01:26:55.934 --> 01:26:57.738
And he still
wears it sometimes,

01:26:57.807 --> 01:26:59.873
even with all the stains,
'cause I got it for him.

01:27:02.182 --> 01:27:04.215
He doesn't know
who I am, Gabriel.

01:27:04.284 --> 01:27:05.945
He just thinks
I'm some random rich guy

01:27:06.013 --> 01:27:08.283
that gave him a bunch of money
and got him a house.

01:27:08.351 --> 01:27:09.950
Why did he let you do that?

01:27:10.019 --> 01:27:13.122
I told him he won a contest
'cause he had a cool mustache.

01:27:13.191 --> 01:27:14.393
-Oh.
-(BOTH CHUCKLING)

01:27:18.064 --> 01:27:20.965
-I like this, too.
-What?

01:27:21.034 --> 01:27:23.829
Being with you, laughing.

01:27:23.897 --> 01:27:26.902
It's one of the best parts
of being human.

01:27:26.970 --> 01:27:28.242
It is.

01:27:30.068 --> 01:27:34.246
I just wish
you had a different angel.

01:27:34.314 --> 01:27:36.780
Azrael would never
have let this happen.

01:27:36.849 --> 01:27:38.341
Who's he?

01:27:38.410 --> 01:27:43.816
(SIGHS) He's a great angel,
has giant wings, guides people.

01:27:43.884 --> 01:27:45.987
-He's a rock star.
-(MUTTERS DISMISSIVELY)

01:27:46.055 --> 01:27:48.852
I think I'd rather
have the guy that's
really into cumbia,

01:27:48.921 --> 01:27:50.691
chicken nuggies
and psychedelics.

01:27:50.760 --> 01:27:53.091
You're just saying that
'cause I'm right here.

01:27:54.096 --> 01:27:56.101
Nope.

01:27:56.170 --> 01:27:58.195
I'm saying it
'cause it's true.

01:27:58.872 --> 01:28:00.634
You're my angel.

01:28:00.703 --> 01:28:02.833
And you're not Azrael.
You're Gabriel.

01:28:02.902 --> 01:28:05.338
And you know what?
I love Gabriel.

01:28:05.407 --> 01:28:06.742
I prefer Gabriel.

01:28:09.213 --> 01:28:10.649
And I'm not Jeff.

01:28:10.717 --> 01:28:12.449
I'm Arj.

01:28:12.517 --> 01:28:14.420
And things aren't
going well right now,

01:28:15.615 --> 01:28:17.222
but I got to try.

01:28:17.291 --> 01:28:19.326
I want to see
where it goes, as me.

01:28:20.859 --> 01:28:22.296
As Arj.

01:28:26.925 --> 01:28:28.995
I think
my life's worth living.

01:28:32.939 --> 01:28:33.967
